  ('ea-a149-coast', 'drive', 'A149 Norfolk Coast Road', 'The classic north Norfolk coast road through flint villages, salt marshes and harbours (Brancaster, Holkham, Wells, Blakeney, Cley, Sheringham). Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.9393, 0.4904), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(0.4904 52.9393, 0.505 52.9509, 0.5316 52.9566, 0.5595 52.9587, 0.5888 52.9596, 0.6179 52.9619, 0.6464 52.9628, 0.6745 52.966, 0.7034 52.9631, 0.7279 52.9555, 0.7507 52.963, 0.7788 52.9601, 0.8063 52.9602, 0.8343 52.9578, 0.8562 52.9521, 0.8825 52.947, 0.9096 52.9502, 0.9363 52.9484, 0.9579 52.9531, 0.985 52.9556, 1.0124 52.9536, 1.0394 52.9527, 1.0644 52.9548, 1.0913 52.9517, 1.1138 52.9427, 1.1412 52.9428, 1.1713 52.9409, 1.2001 52.9422, 1.2267 52.9369, 1.2546 52.9374, 1.2824 52.9336, 1.3012 52.931)'), 37.4, null, 'East Anglia', array['Very busy in summer and at weekends; repeated 30/40 mph village limits and narrow pinch points (Cley, Blakeney, Brancaster); lots of cyclists and walkers; vehicle-ASB PSPO in force in parts of Cromer (North Norfolk DC, from Aug 2024).']::text[]),
  ('ea-a1065-forest', 'drive', 'A1065 through Thetford Forest', 'Sweeping A-road through the pine plantations of Thetford Forest, then open Breckland to Swaffham and on to Fakenham. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.3667, 0.5401), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(0.5401 52.3667, 0.5425 52.3844, 0.5603 52.3968, 0.5798 52.4066, 0.584 52.424, 0.6026 52.4371, 0.6236 52.4484, 0.6333 52.4644, 0.646 52.4799, 0.6519 52.4977, 0.66 52.5139, 0.6657 52.5244, 0.6714 52.5349, 0.6775 52.5522, 0.6883 52.5688, 0.7001 52.5826, 0.6976 52.6004, 0.6924 52.6172, 0.689 52.6344, 0.6888 52.6494, 0.6879 52.6677, 0.6883 52.6851, 0.7015 52.7004, 0.7177 52.7147, 0.7257 52.7311, 0.7403 52.7475, 0.7467 52.765, 0.771 52.774, 0.7945 52.7838, 0.8051 52.8002, 0.8216 52.8145, 0.8374 52.8285, 0.8373 52.8349)'), 37.8, null, 'East Anglia', array['Tree cover limits visibility in places (source); deer and HGVs; town limits and level crossing at Brandon; the STANTA military training area borders the road north of Mundford – no stopping at gates.']::text[]),
  ('ea-b1145', 'drive', 'B1145 trans-Norfolk byway', 'A quiet cross-county B-road from the north-east of Norfolk to King''s Lynn, mixing long straights with tighter village sections. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.831, 1.3895), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(1.3895 52.831, 1.3705 52.824, 1.3474 52.8206, 1.3236 52.819, 1.2995 52.8131, 1.2736 52.8094, 1.2671 52.792, 1.2472 52.787, 1.2232 52.7866, 1.1996 52.7766, 1.1739 52.7692, 1.1474 52.7739, 1.123 52.77, 1.0999 52.7621, 1.0725 52.7594, 1.0455 52.7537, 1.0269 52.7436, 0.9988 52.7444, 0.9702 52.742, 0.9415 52.7451, 0.9154 52.7527, 0.8922 52.7524, 0.8682 52.7457, 0.8415 52.7395, 0.8154 52.7306, 0.7895 52.7236, 0.7622 52.7266, 0.7364 52.733, 0.7143 52.7436, 0.6907 52.7539, 0.6627 52.7585, 0.6355 52.7537, 0.6102 52.7449, 0.5827 52.746, 0.567 52.7553, 0.5383 52.7499, 0.5109 52.7473, 0.4821 52.7503, 0.4527 52.7535, 0.4248 52.757, 0.4041 52.754)'), 49, null, 'East Anglia', array['Pheasants and other wildlife; tall hedges hide the view in low cars; greasy when wet; crosses the A140 at Aylsham.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('ea-suffolk-coast-b', 'drive', 'Suffolk Heritage Coast B-roads', 'Tight, hedge-lined B-roads behind the Suffolk coast via Snape, Leiston, Blythburgh and Southwold, finishing on the B1127 to Beccles. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.0949, 1.5341), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(1.5341 52.0949, 1.5259 52.1111, 1.5035 52.1211, 1.4832 52.1333, 1.4608 52.1423, 1.4618 52.1502, 1.4861 52.1581, 1.5009 52.1718, 1.519 52.1799, 1.5428 52.1831, 1.5643 52.1942, 1.5746 52.2096, 1.582 52.2255, 1.5667 52.2398, 1.5677 52.2534, 1.5808 52.2681, 1.5909 52.2837, 1.5932 52.3009, 1.5991 52.3176, 1.609 52.3312, 1.633 52.3379, 1.66 52.3354, 1.6768 52.3405, 1.677 52.3564, 1.6714 52.372, 1.6714 52.3894, 1.6785 52.4076, 1.6566 52.4163, 1.6324 52.4229, 1.6131 52.4348, 1.5906 52.4432, 1.5688 52.4533, 1.5624 52.4582)'), 38.7, null, 'East Anglia', array['Narrow sections, bumps and cambers; Snape and Leiston slow you down; A1095 into Southwold busy with tourists; Southwold parking very busy in summer.']::text[]),
  ('ea-b1077', 'drive', 'B1077 Ipswich to Attleborough', 'Rural B-road running parallel to the A140 through Debenham, Eye and Diss, alternating hedge-lined bends with open, fast sections. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.0851, 1.1723), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(1.1723 52.0851, 1.1815 52.1011, 1.1874 52.1165, 1.1868 52.1331, 1.1959 52.1483, 1.1976 52.1652, 1.2035 52.181, 1.2032 52.1959, 1.1929 52.2084, 1.1833 52.2216, 1.1825 52.2374, 1.1727 52.2527, 1.1686 52.2694, 1.1516 52.2828, 1.1546 52.2971, 1.1543 52.314, 1.1458 52.3286, 1.1304 52.3408, 1.1312 52.3554, 1.1235 52.3697, 1.1023 52.3768, 1.1007 52.3938, 1.0966 52.4107, 1.0874 52.4253, 1.0732 52.4381, 1.073 52.4548, 1.0624 52.4713, 1.0401 52.4778, 1.0279 52.4912, 1.0278 52.5082, 1.0094 52.5165, 1.0102 52.5178)'), 36.8, null, 'East Anglia', array['First miles out of Ipswich narrow and built-up; awkward A140 crossing with 40 mph limits; mud, tractors and animals.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('ea-two-windmills', 'drive', 'Two Windmills (Suffolk B-roads)', 'A short twisty loop of mid-Suffolk lanes past Helmingham Hall and two windmills, finishing at Framlingham Castle. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.0851, 1.1723), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(1.1723 52.0851, 1.195 52.0905, 1.2058 52.1038, 1.2187 52.118, 1.2338 52.1316, 1.2211 52.1432, 1.2158 52.16, 1.2028 52.1745, 1.2075 52.1902, 1.2097 52.1998, 1.2258 52.2091, 1.2527 52.2172, 1.2762 52.2243, 1.3015 52.2315, 1.3283 52.2276, 1.3415 52.2222)'), 17.9, null, 'East Anglia', array['Congestion around Helmingham Hall events; standing water in places when wet; only fuel stop is Framlingham.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('ea-norfolk-east-coast', 'drive', 'Norfolk east coast road (old B1159)', 'Minor coast road behind the dunes via Winterton, Horsey, Sea Palling, Happisburgh, Mundesley and Overstrand. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.6509, 1.7237), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(1.7237 52.6509, 1.7155 52.667, 1.6997 52.6807, 1.6882 52.6953, 1.6892 52.7109, 1.6738 52.7162, 1.6532 52.7238, 1.6399 52.7396, 1.6447 52.7538, 1.6254 52.7658, 1.6156 52.7795, 1.591 52.7851, 1.5632 52.7834, 1.5488 52.7943, 1.5304 52.8005, 1.5089 52.806, 1.5045 52.8212, 1.5028 52.8381, 1.4829 52.8479, 1.4639 52.8564, 1.4406 52.8641, 1.4355 52.8789, 1.408 52.883, 1.3934 52.896, 1.3675 52.9024, 1.3478 52.9135, 1.3211 52.9201, 1.3025 52.9302, 1.3012 52.931)'), 33.2, null, 'East Anglia', array['Narrow, many 30 mph villages, caravans and summer traffic at Hemsby/Winterton; coastal erosion closures possible near Happisburgh; Great Yarmouth borough has a vehicle-ASB PSPO.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('ea-broads-north', 'drive', 'Northern Broads run', 'Through the heart of the northern Broads via Horning, Ludham and Potter Heigham, past rivers, mills and staithes. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.7126, 1.4106), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(1.4106 52.7126, 1.4366 52.7095, 1.4638 52.7077, 1.4893 52.7005, 1.5146 52.702, 1.5349 52.71, 1.5626 52.7138, 1.5829 52.7102, 1.6005 52.6972, 1.6185 52.6867, 1.6138 52.6708, 1.5957 52.6631, 1.5736 52.6527, 1.5547 52.6403, 1.5481 52.6392)'), 16.1, null, 'East Anglia', array['Hoveton/Wroxham and Potter Heigham very busy in summer; boatyard traffic; many 30/40 mph limits.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('ea-reedham-ferry', 'drive', 'Reedham Ferry crossing', 'Marshland lanes from Acle to Reedham, across the Yare on Norfolk''s last chain ferry, then south through Loddon to Bungay. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.6392, 1.5481), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(1.5481 52.6392, 1.5738 52.6319, 1.6001 52.6242, 1.5866 52.6074, 1.5757 52.5978, 1.5658 52.5874, 1.5684 52.5726, 1.5536 52.5619, 1.5359 52.5494, 1.521 52.537, 1.4967 52.5341, 1.4811 52.527, 1.473 52.5116, 1.4668 52.4949, 1.4547 52.4831, 1.4289 52.4785, 1.438 52.4712, 1.4358 52.4574, 1.4374 52.4562)'), 21.1, null, 'East Anglia', array['Ferry is tolled, small (3 cars) and can stop in very high/low water – check before you go; short stretch of the busy A47 Acle Straight; single-track marsh lanes.']::text[]),
  ('ea-b1108', 'drive', 'B1108 Norwich to Bodney', 'Straightforward rural B-road south-west of Norwich through Hingham and Watton, linking to the A1065 and Thetford Forest. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.6258, 1.2215), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(1.2215 52.6258, 1.2104 52.6243, 1.1818 52.6244, 1.1535 52.6247, 1.1265 52.6218, 1.0995 52.6208, 1.0778 52.6094, 1.0575 52.5985, 1.0388 52.5867, 1.0152 52.5786, 0.987 52.579, 0.9606 52.5769, 0.932 52.5704, 0.9053 52.5701, 0.8774 52.5705, 0.8479 52.5706, 0.8233 52.5703, 0.7967 52.5669, 0.7683 52.5648, 0.7451 52.5556, 0.7162 52.5559, 0.6982 52.5553)'), 25.7, null, 'East Anglia', array['Watton town traffic; village limits; military land near Bodney – no stopping at gates.']::text[]),
  ('ea-lowestoft-southwold', 'drive', 'Lowestoft to Southwold', 'Short coastal link from Britain''s most easterly town down the A12 to Wrentham, then the B1127 into Southwold. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.4524, 1.727), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(1.727 52.4524, 1.7237 52.4417, 1.7086 52.4236, 1.6854 52.4136, 1.6715 52.3979, 1.6715 52.3806, 1.6747 52.3647, 1.6819 52.3488, 1.6742 52.3332, 1.6793 52.3261)'), 10.6, null, 'East Anglia', array['A12 single carriageway with HGVs; Kessingland limits; Southwold busy in summer.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('ea-p-ness-point', 'photo', 'Ness Point, Lowestoft', 'Britain''s most easterly point, with the Euroscope marker and wind turbine. Unique "most easterly" landmark.', private.pt(52.4812, 1.7627), null, null, null, 'East Anglia', array['Industrial approach; park in the town car parks (Hamilton Road) and walk – don''t block the access road.']::text[]),
  ('ea-p-southwold-pier', 'photo', 'Southwold Pier & North Parade', 'Pier, beach huts and seafront; the pier car park and North Road parking are a short walk away. Well-known Suffolk seaside backdrop.', private.pt(52.3304, 1.6868), null, null, null, 'East Anglia', array['Very busy in summer; pay parking; North Parade is narrow.']::text[]),
  ('ea-p-dunwich-heath', 'photo', 'Dunwich Heath (Coastguard Cottages)', 'National Trust clifftop car park on the heath, purple heather in late summer. NT car park with sea and heath views.', private.pt(52.252, 1.628), null, null, null, 'East Anglia', array['NT car park charges for non-members; check closing times.']::text[]),
  ('ea-p-scallop', 'photo', 'The Scallop, Aldeburgh', 'Maggi Hambling''s steel shell sculpture on the shingle north of Aldeburgh; car park on Thorpe Road nearby. Distinctive sculpture and big skies.', private.pt(52.1605, 1.6058), null, null, null, 'East Anglia', array['Car park only – never drive on the shingle; busy at weekends.']::text[]),
  ('ea-p-orford-quay', 'photo', 'Orford Quay', 'Quay car park on the River Ore looking towards Orford Ness. Quiet riverside backdrop at the end of the Suffolk coast route.', private.pt(52.0909, 1.5392), null, null, null, 'East Anglia', array['Pay car park; small and busy on summer weekends.']::text[]),
  ('ea-p-framlingham', 'photo', 'Framlingham Castle', 'English Heritage castle with its own car park, at the end of the Two Windmills route. Named point on the Porsche Roads route.', private.pt(52.2242, 1.3467), null, null, null, 'East Anglia', array['EH opening hours; car park charge for non-members.']::text[]),
  ('ea-p-saxtead', 'photo', 'Saxtead Green Post Mill', 'Restored post mill beside the A1120 on the village green. Porsche Roads calls it ''a good convoy photo spot''.', private.pt(52.2319, 1.2984), null, null, null, 'East Anglia', array['Park considerately; don''t drive on the green; A1120 traffic.']::text[]),
  ('ea-p-horsey', 'photo', 'Horsey Windpump', 'National Trust drainage mill beside Horsey Mere, with a car park. Iconic Broads windmill on the east coast road.', private.pt(52.7411, 1.639), null, null, null, 'East Anglia', array['NT car park charges; busy in seal season (Nov–Feb).']::text[]),
  ('ea-p-st-benets', 'photo', 'St Benet''s Abbey', 'Ruined abbey gatehouse with a windmill built into it, on the marshes by the River Bure. Classic Broads landmark.', private.pt(52.6861, 1.5251), null, null, null, 'East Anglia', array['Narrow single-track access lane with a small car park; soft verges.']::text[]),
  ('ea-p-happisburgh', 'photo', 'Happisburgh Lighthouse', 'Red-and-white striped lighthouse, the only independently run lighthouse in Britain. Striking backdrop on the east coast road.', private.pt(52.8205, 1.537), null, null, null, 'East Anglia', array['Lighthouse Lane is narrow – use the village car park; erosion closures near the cliff.']::text[]),
  ('ea-p-cromer-pier', 'photo', 'Cromer Pier & clifftop', 'Victorian pier below the town, with clifftop viewpoints. End point of both coast routes.', private.pt(52.9337, 1.3014), null, null, null, 'East Anglia', array['Pay car parks; North Norfolk vehicle-ASB PSPO covers parts of Cromer – no gatherings or revving.']::text[]),
  ('ea-p-hunstanton', 'photo', 'Old Hunstanton lighthouse & cliffs', 'Clifftop car park by the old lighthouse above the striped cliffs; west-facing sunsets over the Wash. Start of the A149 coast road; Biker Guide notes plenty of parking at the Cliff Top café.', private.pt(52.9513, 0.4963), null, null, null, 'East Anglia', array['Pay parking; busy summer evenings.']::text[]),
  ('ea-p-holkham', 'photo', 'Lady Anne''s Drive, Holkham', 'Estate-run drive and parking leading to Holkham beach and pinewoods. Famous beach access off the A149.', private.pt(52.9646, 0.8145), null, null, null, 'East Anglia', array['Private estate road with paid parking; strictly no gatherings; very busy in summer.']::text[]),
  ('ea-p-blakeney', 'photo', 'Blakeney Quay', 'Quayside car park on the salt marshes, with boats and big skies. Popular north Norfolk harbour.', private.pt(52.9558, 1.0164), null, null, null, 'East Anglia', array['The quay car park floods on high spring tides – check tide times; pay parking.']::text[]),
  ('ea-p-high-lodge', 'photo', 'High Lodge, Thetford Forest', 'Forestry England visitor centre deep in Thetford Forest, reached by a forest drive. Tall pines and forest roads.', private.pt(52.4345, 0.6632), null, null, null, 'East Anglia', array['Paid entry/parking; gates close at set times; 10–20 mph on site.']::text[]),
  ('k-alkham-valley', 'drive', 'Alkham Valley Road', 'Short, flowing valley road through Alkham between Folkestone and Dover, used by local riders instead of the A20. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.1115, 1.1873), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(1.1873 51.1115, 1.2014 51.1215, 1.2153 51.1319, 1.2351 51.1388, 1.2564 51.1456, 1.2688 51.1477)'), 4.7, null, 'Kent', array['Reviewers say 40/50 mph limits now cover most of it and police are seen more; a couple of bends and junctions have poor visibility.']::text[]),
  ('k-stone-street', 'drive', 'Stone Street (B2068)', 'Arrow-straight Roman road over the North Downs with crests and dips, via Stelling Minnis and Petham. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.1023, 1.0458), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(1.0458 51.1023, 1.0436 51.116, 1.0477 51.1273, 1.0506 51.1429, 1.0513 51.1578, 1.0529 51.1724, 1.0547 51.188, 1.0577 51.2026, 1.0604 51.2172, 1.0625 51.2323, 1.0779 51.2428, 1.0863 51.2565, 1.0929 51.2684)'), 12.3, null, 'Kent', array['Staggered crossroads (source); the long straights invite speed – keep it legal; farm traffic.']::text[]),
  ('k-romney-marsh', 'drive', 'Romney Marsh coast', 'Flat, open marsh roads from Hythe along the Dymchurch coast to New Romney and Lydd, then past the ranges to Camber. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.0689, 1.0844), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(1.0844 51.0689, 1.0657 51.0672, 1.0475 51.059, 1.0349 51.0477, 1.0178 51.0377, 0.9995 51.03, 0.9832 51.0232, 0.9613 51.0233, 0.9519 51.0124, 0.9479 50.9983, 0.9406 50.986, 0.9222 50.9849, 0.9231 50.9706, 0.9163 50.957, 0.899 50.9479, 0.879 50.9424, 0.86 50.9339, 0.8392 50.9346)'), 17.4, null, 'Kent', array['Police presence across the marsh (source); Lydd ranges – obey red flags and don''t stop; Dymchurch seafront busy in summer.']::text[]),
  ('k-dungeness', 'drive', 'Dungeness coast road', 'Coast Drive past Greatstone to the shingle headland at Dungeness, with its lighthouses and black huts, returning inland to Lydd. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(50.9849, 0.9432), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(0.9432 50.9849, 0.9628 50.9827, 0.9631 50.9703, 0.9643 50.9556, 0.9701 50.9398, 0.9574 50.933, 0.9359 50.9388, 0.918 50.9485, 0.9064 50.951)'), 7.9, null, 'Kent', array['Dungeness is a privately owned estate and nature reserve – stay on the road and in car parks, never drive on the shingle; homes there are private; don''t stop at the power station gates.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('k-countryside-loop', 'drive', 'Kentish countryside loop', 'Weald loop via Lamberhurst, Newenden, Tenterden, Biddenden and Goudhurst on the A21, A28 and A262. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.1955, 0.2751), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(0.2751 51.1955, 0.279 51.1846, 0.2964 51.175, 0.3062 51.1624, 0.3035 51.148, 0.3228 51.1397, 0.3452 51.1367, 0.3593 51.1265, 0.3747 51.1185, 0.3942 51.1117, 0.404 51.1011, 0.3992 51.0887, 0.4179 51.0802, 0.4317 51.0694, 0.4468 51.0586, 0.4464 51.0452, 0.4597 51.0337, 0.4748 51.0257, 0.4974 51.0275, 0.5185 51.0269, 0.5313 51.0386, 0.5309 51.0423, 0.549 51.0344, 0.5671 51.0258, 0.5908 51.0217, 0.608 51.0243, 0.6139 51.038, 0.6287 51.0489, 0.643 51.0576, 0.6618 51.0654, 0.684 51.0672, 0.701 51.0678, 0.7017 51.0691, 0.6947 51.081, 0.6785 51.0876, 0.6699 51.0965, 0.6535 51.1037, 0.643 51.113, 0.624 51.1152, 0.603 51.116, 0.5826 51.1096, 0.5598 51.109, 0.5385 51.1109, 0.5165 51.1119, 0.4937 51.1099, 0.4712 51.1138, 0.4506 51.1107, 0.43 51.1113, 0.4075 51.1112, 0.3868 51.1144, 0.3692 51.1223, 0.3562 51.1314, 0.3367 51.1384, 0.316 51.1436, 0.3029 51.1495, 0.3059 51.1646, 0.2933 51.1761, 0.283 51.1806, 0.2709 51.1912, 0.2751 51.1955)'), 59.3, null, 'Kent', array['Patchy repairs; speed cameras in villages; police most likely at Tenterden, Hawkhurst and on the A21; weekend traffic.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('k-white-cliffs-coast', 'drive', 'White Cliffs to Deal', 'Up out of Dover past the castle to St Margaret''s at Cliffe and Kingsdown, then along the front to Walmer and Deal. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.1251, 1.3133), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(1.3133 51.1251, 1.3245 51.1255, 1.3313 51.1368, 1.3399 51.1497, 1.3601 51.1546, 1.361 51.1623, 1.366 51.1737, 1.3797 51.1848, 1.4019 51.1855, 1.4023 51.1997, 1.4024 51.2128, 1.4 51.2229, 1.4027 51.2242)'), 11.5, null, 'Kent', array['St Margaret''s Bay hill is steep and narrow; Deal seafront busy in summer.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('k-folkestone-dover-clifftop', 'drive', 'Folkestone–Dover clifftop (B2011)', 'The old clifftop road via Capel-le-Ferne and the Battle of Britain Memorial, with Channel views, dropping into Dover on the A20. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.0801, 1.1875), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(1.1875 51.0801, 1.1901 51.0906, 1.1991 51.0964, 1.2193 51.1034, 1.2413 51.1048, 1.2618 51.1116, 1.2821 51.1178, 1.3018 51.1245, 1.3158 51.1263, 1.3133 51.1251)'), 8.2, null, 'Kent', array['Clifftop gusts; Capel-le-Ferne 30 mph; A20 into Dover carries port freight traffic.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('k-thanet-coast', 'drive', 'Thanet coast', 'Along the north Kent coast from Herne Bay past Reculver Towers to Margate, Broadstairs and Ramsgate. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.3725, 1.1307), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(1.1307 51.3725, 1.1472 51.3713, 1.1652 51.3699, 1.1852 51.3717, 1.2043 51.3647, 1.2283 51.3607, 1.2527 51.3584, 1.2749 51.3589, 1.2951 51.3651, 1.3111 51.375, 1.3328 51.3788, 1.3556 51.3799, 1.3743 51.3862, 1.3926 51.3868, 1.4138 51.3813, 1.4343 51.3812, 1.446 51.3763, 1.4424 51.3621, 1.4397 51.352, 1.4299 51.3404, 1.4197 51.3335)'), 20.2, null, 'Kent', array['Margate/Broadstairs seafronts slow and busy in summer; 20 mph zones; parking charges.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('k-p-dungeness', 'photo', 'Dungeness Old Lighthouse', 'Old and new lighthouses, the light railway and black huts on the shingle; parking by the old lighthouse. Much-photographed, otherworldly landscape.', private.pt(50.9137, 0.9697), null, null, null, 'Kent', array['Private estate and nature reserve – park only in marked areas, never on the shingle; respect private homes.']::text[]),
  ('k-p-samphire-hoe', 'photo', 'Samphire Hoe', 'Country park made from Channel Tunnel spoil, reached through a traffic-light-controlled tunnel from the A20. Under the white cliffs with sea views.', private.pt(51.1049, 1.2753), null, null, null, 'Kent', array['Single-lane access tunnel; pay car park; gates close in the evening.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('k-p-white-cliffs', 'photo', 'White Cliffs of Dover (Langdon Cliffs)', 'National Trust car park and visitor centre on the clifftop overlooking Dover port. Views over the cliffs and ferries.', private.pt(51.1316, 1.3375), null, null, null, 'Kent', array['Car park 07:00–19:00; charge for non-members (£5–6).']::text[]),
  ('k-p-bob-memorial', 'photo', 'Battle of Britain Memorial, Capel-le-Ferne', 'Clifftop memorial with Spitfire and Hurricane replicas and a visitor car park. On the B2011 clifftop route.', private.pt(51.0985, 1.206), null, null, null, 'Kent', array['Respectful memorial site – no meets.']::text[]),
  ('k-p-st-margarets', 'photo', 'St Margaret''s Bay', 'Small shingle bay under the cliffs with a beach car park. Quiet cove on the White Cliffs to Deal route.', private.pt(51.1509, 1.3856), null, null, null, 'Kent', array['Steep, narrow hill down; small car park fills fast.']::text[]),
  ('k-p-reculver', 'photo', 'Reculver Towers', 'Twin towers of a ruined church on the coast, with a country park car park. Landmark on the Thanet coast route.', private.pt(51.3795, 1.1997), null, null, null, 'Kent', array['Pay car park; exposed in bad weather.']::text[]),
  ('k-p-botany-bay', 'photo', 'Botany Bay, Kingsgate', 'Chalk stacks and sandy bay; clifftop car park on Botany Road. Classic Thanet coastline.', private.pt(51.3884, 1.434), null, null, null, 'Kent', array['Pay parking; busy summer weekends.']::text[]),
  ('k-p-folkestone-harbour', 'photo', 'Folkestone Harbour Arm', 'Restored harbour arm and old station with food stalls; harbour parking nearby. Industrial-chic seafront backdrop.', private.pt(51.0762, 1.1925), null, null, null, 'Kent', array['Pay parking; events at weekends.']::text[]),
  ('k-p-bluebell-hill', 'photo', 'Bluebell Hill picnic site', 'Kent County Council picnic site and viewpoint over the Medway valley. Elevated view near Chatham.', private.pt(51.3315, 0.5012), null, null, null, 'Kent', array['Check closing times; no meets; A229 junctions are fast.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('k-p-chatham-dockyard', 'photo', 'Historic Dockyard Chatham', 'Georgian dockyard and film location with paid visitor parking. Period buildings and cobbles (with permission).', private.pt(51.3949, 0.5283), null, null, null, 'Kent', array['Ticketed site; commercial/car shoots need permission.']::text[]),
  ('l-embankment-night', 'drive', 'Embankment & Tower Bridge night loop', 'Classic after-dark loop: Victoria Embankment and Upper/Lower Thames Street east to Tower Bridge, back along the South Bank to Westminster Bridge. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.501, -0.125), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-0.125 51.501, -0.1226 51.5063, -0.1165 51.5104, -0.1072 51.511, -0.0968 51.5112, -0.0968 51.5111, -0.0968 51.5112, -0.0878 51.5098, -0.0786 51.5096, -0.074 51.5087, -0.0769 51.5032, -0.0794 51.502, -0.0832 51.5046, -0.0908 51.5047, -0.0973 51.5052, -0.1058 51.5072, -0.1108 51.5071, -0.1134 51.5045, -0.1165 51.5004, -0.1218 51.5008)'), 7.7, null, 'London', array['ULEZ applies 24/7 (non-compliant vehicles pay daily). Congestion Charge (£18/day from Jan 2026) applies Mon–Fri 07:00–18:00 and Sat/Sun/bank holidays 12:00–18:00 – run it after 18:00. 20 mph limits on most central roads; red routes = no stopping. Westminster/K&C High Court injunction and PSPO: no racing, stunts, revving or organised meets – revving/dangerous driving penalties apply 18:00–07:00. Tower Bridge closes for lifts.']::text[]),
  ('l-chelsea-battersea', 'drive', 'Chelsea & Battersea river loop', 'West along Grosvenor Road and Chelsea Embankment, over Battersea Bridge and back past Battersea Power Station and Nine Elms. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.4931, -0.126), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-0.126 51.4931, -0.1292 51.4888, -0.136 51.4855, -0.144 51.4864, -0.1524 51.4853, -0.161 51.4846, -0.1694 51.483, -0.1708 51.4792, -0.1653 51.4748, -0.1562 51.4753, -0.1486 51.4762, -0.1433 51.4791, -0.1357 51.4817, -0.1318 51.4835, -0.1242 51.4861, -0.122 51.4916, -0.1211 51.494, -0.126 51.4931)'), 6.9, null, 'London', array['ULEZ applies 24/7 (non-compliant vehicles pay daily). Congestion Charge (£18/day from Jan 2026) applies Mon–Fri 07:00–18:00 and Sat/Sun/bank holidays 12:00–18:00 – run it after 18:00. 20 mph limits on most central roads; red routes = no stopping.']::text[]),
  ('l-isle-of-dogs', 'drive', 'Canary Wharf & Isle of Dogs loop', 'Through the Limehouse Link tunnel to Westferry Circus, round the Isle of Dogs on Westferry and Manchester Roads, back via Aspen Way. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.5086, -0.0319), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-0.0319 51.5086, -0.0234 51.5088, -0.0142 51.5072, -0.0091 51.5073, -0.0184 51.5075, -0.0266 51.509, -0.0264 51.5056, -0.025 51.5005, -0.0163 51.5002, -0.0088 51.5011, -0.0077 51.5067, -0.0164 51.507, -0.0072 51.5077, 0.0002 51.5107, -0.0047 51.5081, -0.0139 51.5071, -0.0229 51.5086, -0.0316 51.5082, -0.0381 51.5116, -0.0385 51.5115, -0.0319 51.5086)'), 8.2, null, 'London', array['Canary Wharf estate roads are private and patrolled – no stopping or filming there without permission; no stopping in the tunnel; 20 mph in Tower Hamlets. ULEZ applies (outside the Congestion Charge zone).']::text[]),
  ('l-royal-docks-woolwich', 'drive', 'Royal Docks & Woolwich Ferry', 'Past Royal Victoria and Royal Albert Docks and London City Airport, across the Thames on the free Woolwich Ferry, back west to the Peninsula. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.5111, 0.0131), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(0.0131 51.5111, 0.0144 51.5079, 0.0201 51.5043, 0.0282 51.5048, 0.0314 51.5024, 0.0396 51.5041, 0.0405 51.5095, 0.0542 51.5089, 0.0634 51.5086, 0.0713 51.5079, 0.0703 51.5023, 0.0636 51.5, 0.0624 51.4978, 0.0617 51.4937, 0.0646 51.4938, 0.0556 51.4929, 0.0478 51.4903, 0.0415 51.4874, 0.0331 51.4866, 0.0275 51.4899, 0.0183 51.4904, 0.0103 51.4928, 0.008 51.495)'), 8.9, null, 'London', array['Ferry runs daytime/early evening only and can be suspended for fog or tides (check TfL); ULEZ applies; Blackwall and Silvertown tunnels nearby are tolled during the day.']::text[]),
  ('l-westway', 'drive', 'Westway (A40) elevated', 'The elevated A40 Westway from Paddington to White City, at its best at night with the city lights below. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.5224, -0.1619), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-0.1619 51.5224, -0.1687 51.5201, -0.1789 51.5201, -0.1886 51.5195, -0.1974 51.5212, -0.2063 51.5192, -0.215 51.5162, -0.2238 51.5151, -0.2248 51.5149)'), 3.4, null, 'London', array['Speed cameras; no stopping; ULEZ applies.']::text[]),
  ('l-p-battersea', 'photo', 'Battersea Power Station', 'Restored power station and riverside; use the on-site car park. Iconic chimneys and river views.', private.pt(51.4818, -0.1446), null, null, null, 'London', array['Private estate – security may stop filming; ULEZ.']::text[]),
  ('l-p-greenwich-peninsula', 'photo', 'Greenwich Peninsula / The O2', 'Riverside around the O2 with Canary Wharf across the water; O2 car parks. Skyline views at night.', private.pt(51.5029, 0.0032), null, null, null, 'London', array['Private estate in parts; Blackwall/Silvertown tunnels tolled in the day; ULEZ.']::text[]),
  ('l-p-royal-victoria-dock', 'photo', 'Royal Victoria Dock', 'Dockside with cable car and ExCeL; use the ExCeL or dockside car parks. Wide open waterside views.', private.pt(51.5066, 0.0284), null, null, null, 'London', array['Busy during ExCeL events; ULEZ.']::text[]),
  ('l-p-canary-wharf', 'photo', 'Canary Wharf (Canada Square)', 'Glass towers and lit-up plazas; park in the estate car parks. Classic night-time city backdrop.', private.pt(51.5051, -0.0178), null, null, null, 'London', array['Private estate: security stops unauthorised filming and stopping; no gatherings.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('l-p-tower-bridge', 'photo', 'Tower Bridge from Potters Fields', 'Shoot Tower Bridge from the Potters Fields riverside; the bridge itself is a no-stopping red route. London''s most recognisable bridge.', private.pt(51.5042, -0.0784), null, null, null, 'London', array['No stopping on the bridge or approaches; pay parking nearby; 20 mph; Congestion Charge in the day.']::text[]),
  ('l-p-westminster-bridge', 'photo', 'Westminster Bridge & Parliament', 'Rolling or pavement shots of cars with Big Ben behind. Iconic London backdrop.', private.pt(51.5009, -0.1218), null, null, null, 'London', array['No stopping (red route); Westminster car-meet injunction/PSPO – no gatherings or revving; Congestion Charge in the day.']::text[]),
  ('l-p-embankment', 'photo', 'Victoria Embankment', 'Lamp-lined riverside road with views to the London Eye; good for moving shots. Classic night-run backdrop.', private.pt(51.5102, -0.1172), null, null, null, 'London', array['No stopping on the red route – use nearby paid car parks; Westminster PSPO 18:00–07:00 for revving/anti-social driving.']::text[]),
  ('l-p-ally-pally', 'photo', 'Alexandra Palace terrace', 'Hilltop palace with a panoramic view over London; on-site car parks. One of the best free skyline views.', private.pt(51.595, -0.1289), null, null, null, 'London', array['Park in marked bays only; no meets; events can close car parks.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('l-p-greenwich-park', 'photo', 'Greenwich Park (General Wolfe viewpoint)', 'Viewpoint over Queen''s House and Canary Wharf; Blackheath Avenue car park alongside. Classic London panorama.', private.pt(51.4777, -0.0004), null, null, null, 'London', array['Royal Parks car park is pay-and-display and closes with the park at dusk.']::text[]),
  ('l-p-thames-barrier', 'photo', 'Thames Barrier Park', 'Landscaped park looking out to the Thames Barrier gates. Unusual industrial-river backdrop.', private.pt(51.5007, 0.0342), null, null, null, 'London', array['Park opening hours; limited parking nearby; ULEZ.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('l-p-olympic-park', 'photo', 'Queen Elizabeth Olympic Park (Orbit)', 'ArcelorMittal Orbit, London Stadium and modern architecture; park car parks. Modern architecture backdrop.', private.pt(51.5383, -0.013), null, null, null, 'London', array['Event-day closures; private estate rules on filming.']::text[]),
  ('l-p-richmond-hill', 'photo', 'Richmond Hill viewpoint', 'Protected view over the Thames towards Twickenham. Famous protected view.', private.pt(51.4542, -0.2999), null, null, null, 'London', array['Limited roadside parking – use local pay car parks; residents nearby, no gatherings.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('ne-honister', 'drive', 'Honister Pass (B5289)', 'Up Borrowdale past Seatoller and over Honister Pass, past the slate mine at the top, then down to Gatesgarth and along Buttermere. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(54.5471, -3.1577), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-3.1577 54.5471, -3.1536 54.5346, -3.1469 54.5201, -3.1675 54.5136, -3.1917 54.5128, -3.212 54.5193, -3.2377 54.5228, -3.2571 54.5316, -3.2769 54.5414)'), 9, null, 'Lake District', array['Gradients up to 1 in 4 (25%) with tight bends between stone walls; narrow, so expect to reverse for oncoming traffic; very busy with tourists, cyclists and walkers in summer; sheep on the open fell; can close or be impassable in snow and ice.']::text[]),
  ('ne-newlands', 'drive', 'Newlands Pass', 'Unclassified mountain road from Braithwaite up the Newlands valley to Newlands Hause, then a steep drop to Buttermere village. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(54.6019, -3.1903), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-3.1903 54.6019, -3.1884 54.5897, -3.1863 54.5745, -3.2055 54.5651, -3.2264 54.5591, -3.2461 54.548, -3.2705 54.5438, -3.2767 54.5412)'), 7, null, 'Lake District', array['Gradients of 1 in 4 on both sides; very narrow with few passing places in places; unfenced drops; tourists, cyclists and walkers; sheep; not gritted as a priority in winter.']::text[]),
  ('ne-whinlatter', 'drive', 'Whinlatter Pass (B5292)', 'Wooded climb from Braithwaite through Whinlatter Forest, past the visitor centre, then open views down to the Lorton valley. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(54.6022, -3.1925), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-3.1925 54.6022, -3.2095 54.6085, -3.2343 54.6093, -3.2613 54.6117, -3.2805 54.6197, -3.3013 54.6194)'), 5.5, null, 'Lake District', array['Hairpins and a steep start out of Braithwaite; Whinlatter Forest visitor traffic and cyclists; forest car parks are pay and display.']::text[]),
  ('ne-a684-garsdale', 'drive', 'A684 Garsdale (Hawes to Sedbergh)', 'West from Hawes up Wensleydale to Garsdale Head, then down the long, narrow valley of Garsdale to Sedbergh. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(54.3042, -2.1965), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-2.1965 54.3042, -2.2172 54.3111, -2.2357 54.3198, -2.2596 54.3255, -2.2879 54.3261, -2.3147 54.3291, -2.3366 54.3192, -2.3559 54.3085, -2.3796 54.3025, -2.4044 54.3011, -2.426 54.3091, -2.4516 54.3114, -2.4775 54.3164, -2.5025 54.3201, -2.5284 54.3236)'), 15.7, null, 'Yorkshire Dales', array['Stone walls tight to the road and limited sightlines; farm traffic and mud, slippery in the wet; sheep; Hawes is busy on summer weekends.']::text[]),
  ('ne-b6270-swaledale', 'drive', 'B6270 Swaledale', 'Over the moor from Nateby to Keld at the head of Swaledale, then down the dale through Thwaite, Muker, Gunnerside and Low Row to Reeth. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(54.4558, -2.3491), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-2.3491 54.4558, -2.3275 54.4485, -2.3062 54.4387, -2.2863 54.4284, -2.2642 54.4217, -2.2453 54.4103, -2.2195 54.4092, -2.194 54.4077, -2.1688 54.4046, -2.1735 54.3955, -2.1713 54.3804, -2.1481 54.3761, -2.1224 54.3739, -2.0958 54.3743, -2.0752 54.3794, -2.0498 54.3733, -2.0252 54.3793, -1.9995 54.3818, -1.9759 54.3861, -1.9494 54.389, -1.9421 54.3894)'), 21.6, null, 'Yorkshire Dales', array['Single-track in places on the moor with passing places; cattle grids; sheep and lambs on the road; gravel and dung; narrow village sections; busy with walkers in summer.']::text[]),
  ('ne-fleet-moss', 'drive', 'Fleet Moss (Hawes to Buckden)', 'From Hawes through Gayle and up over Fleet Moss, then down Langstrothdale past Oughtershaw and Hubberholme to Buckden in Wharfedale. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(54.3042, -2.1965), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-2.1965 54.3042, -2.1995 54.2977, -2.2125 54.284, -2.2114 54.2676, -2.2138 54.2535, -2.2129 54.2399, -2.1979 54.2277, -2.1824 54.2169, -2.1587 54.2108, -2.138 54.2016, -2.1117 54.2003, -2.0913 54.1936, -2.0904 54.1904)'), 12.6, null, 'Yorkshire Dales', array['Very steep sections on the Gayle side; narrow, mostly single-track with passing places in Langstrothdale; cattle grids and free-roaming sheep; exposed and often icy or foggy – avoid in winter.', 'Medium confidence: the line or the source is partial (see the research notes). Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('ne-b6255-ribblehead', 'drive', 'B6255 Ingleton to Hawes (Ribblehead)', 'Up Chapel-le-Dale past White Scar Cave to the Ribblehead Viaduct, then over Newby Head and down into Wensleydale at Hawes. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(54.1539, -2.4679), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-2.4679 54.1539, -2.4494 54.1597, -2.4301 54.1725, -2.4094 54.1832, -2.3904 54.1956, -2.3683 54.205, -2.3453 54.213, -2.3263 54.2234, -2.3154 54.2373, -2.3141 54.2534, -2.2962 54.2659, -2.2807 54.2787, -2.2606 54.2896, -2.2393 54.2991, -2.2131 54.3023, -2.1965 54.3042)'), 16.5, null, 'Yorkshire Dales', array['Large police presence in summer (BestBikingRoads); lambs and sheep in spring; elevation changes and crests near Hawes; visitors stopping at the viaduct; part of the Devil''s Bridge riding area where locals have campaigned about speed and noise.']::text[]),
  ('ne-a59-blubberhouses', 'drive', 'A59 over Blubberhouses Moor', 'The A59 west of Harrogate over Blubberhouses Moor, past Thruscross and down to Bolton Bridge near Bolton Abbey. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(54.0012, -1.6677), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-1.6677 54.0012, -1.6979 53.9973, -1.7238 53.9929, -1.7441 53.9939, -1.7749 53.9972, -1.7986 53.9907, -1.8251 53.9879, -1.8518 53.9849, -1.8714 53.9741, -1.8967 53.9726, -1.9079 53.9761)'), 11.1, null, 'Yorkshire Dales', array['Busy main road with HGVs; 50/60 mph limits and cameras; frequent police patrols at weekends (BestBikingRoads); exposed to fog and snow on the moor; Route 59 café stop at Bolton Abbey.']::text[]),
  ('ne-woodhead', 'drive', 'Woodhead Pass (A628)', 'The Pennine trunk road from Tintwistle along the Longdendale reservoirs and over the Woodhead Pass to the Flouch roundabout. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(53.4721, -1.9734), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-1.9734 53.4721, -1.9497 53.4781, -1.9262 53.4841, -1.9015 53.4863, -1.8788 53.493, -1.8543 53.4957, -1.8286 53.4954, -1.8038 53.494, -1.7834 53.4998, -1.7563 53.4995, -1.7363 53.5058)'), 11, null, 'Peak District', array['Very heavy HGV traffic and frequently congested; described as dangerous (Wikipedia); often closed by snow or high winds; speed cameras; Tintwistle and Hollingworth are 30 mph.']::text[]),
  ('ne-holme-moss', 'drive', 'Holme Moss (A6024)', 'From Holmfirth up through Holme and over Holme Moss past the transmitter mast, then down the hairpins to the Longdendale valley. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(53.5704, -1.787), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-1.787 53.5704, -1.8091 53.5616, -1.8303 53.5531, -1.8468 53.5445, -1.8545 53.5331, -1.8529 53.5243, -1.8535 53.5087, -1.8635 53.4954, -1.8408 53.4958, -1.8339 53.4962)'), 9.2, null, 'Peak District', array['Often the first road in the area blocked by snow; steep (up to 11%) with hairpins and a sheer drop on one side; blind brow at the summit – no overtaking; sheep; poor surface out of Holmfirth (BestBikingRoads); Kirklees nuisance-vehicle PSPO covers the Holmfirth end.']::text[]),
  ('ne-a169-moors', 'drive', 'A169 Pickering to Whitby', 'North across the North York Moors past the Hole of Horcum and RAF Fylingdales, then down Blue Bank to Sleights and on to Whitby. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(54.2456, -0.7767), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-0.7767 54.2456, -0.7531 54.2532, -0.7285 54.2615, -0.7146 54.275, -0.7041 54.2889, -0.6955 54.3037, -0.6913 54.3204, -0.6944 54.3352, -0.6864 54.3495, -0.6844 54.3661, -0.6826 54.3814, -0.6773 54.397, -0.6849 54.4138, -0.6736 54.4301, -0.6627 54.4448, -0.6634 54.4589, -0.6569 54.4736, -0.6588 54.4773)'), 18.6, null, 'North York Moors', array['Busy with coast traffic on summer weekends; the Saltergate bend at the Hole of Horcum is tight; Blue Bank is a steep descent; sheep on the open moor; police patrols in summer.']::text[]),
  ('ne-blakey-ridge', 'drive', 'Blakey Ridge (Hutton-le-Hole to Castleton)', 'Minor road along the top of Blakey Ridge, past the Lion Inn, between Farndale and Rosedale, dropping into Esk Dale at Castleton. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(54.3005, -0.9189), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-0.9189 54.3005, -0.9308 54.3147, -0.935 54.3304, -0.9401 54.3459, -0.9446 54.3608, -0.9482 54.3765, -0.9566 54.3913, -0.9602 54.4067, -0.9492 54.4216, -0.9443 54.4378, -0.95 54.4544, -0.9403 54.4634)'), 12.2, null, 'North York Moors', array['Free-roaming sheep across the whole ridge; walkers; often poor condition; cattle grids; police seen near the A171 end (BestBikingRoads); avoid Rosedale Chimney Bank (1 in 3) off this route.']::text[]),
  ('ne-trough-of-bowland', 'drive', 'Trough of Bowland', 'Through the Forest of Bowland from Dunsop Bridge up the Trough to the summit, then across the moor past Jubilee Tower and down to Lancaster. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(53.9458, -2.5183), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-2.5183 53.9458, -2.5425 53.9504, -2.5652 53.9581, -2.576 53.9715, -2.5979 53.9793, -2.6056 53.9807, -2.6269 53.9756, -2.6442 53.9845, -2.6663 53.9933, -2.686 54.0034, -2.7049 54.0136, -2.7265 54.0229, -2.7495 54.0287, -2.7685 54.0375, -2.7901 54.048)'), 15.7, null, 'Lancashire', array['Steep, narrow and twisty; unfenced moorland with sheep and cattle grids; popular with cyclists and walkers; few passing places near the summit; not a priority for gritting.']::text[]),
  ('ne-a6-shap', 'drive', 'A6 over Shap', 'The old main road north over Shap Fell, the route the M6 replaced: a long climb from Kendal to Shap Summit, then Shap village and on to Penrith. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(54.342, -2.735), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-2.735 54.342, -2.7271 54.3537, -2.7242 54.3695, -2.7317 54.3828, -2.7159 54.3953, -2.6977 54.4046, -2.6973 54.4184, -2.691 54.4323, -2.6897 54.4477, -2.6909 54.4588, -2.6732 54.4702, -2.673 54.4861, -2.6712 54.5019, -2.6698 54.5178, -2.678 54.532, -2.6838 54.5482, -2.6875 54.5641, -2.6958 54.5791, -2.701 54.5948, -2.7165 54.6075, -2.7162 54.6234, -2.7272 54.6377, -2.7403 54.65)'), 24.7, null, 'Cumbria', array['Exposed and often impassable in snow (Wikipedia); camera van reported near Kendal and police on the fast sections (BestBikingRoads); quarry lorries near Shap.']::text[]),
  ('ne-military-road', 'drive', 'Military Road (B6318) along Hadrian''s Wall', 'The 18th-century Military Road west along Hadrian''s Wall, past Brocolitia, Housesteads, The Sill and Cawfields. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(55.031, -2.1285), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-2.1285 55.031, -2.1511 55.0289, -2.1775 55.0344, -2.2093 55.0368, -2.2371 55.0341, -2.266 55.0305, -2.2935 55.0236, -2.3195 55.0115, -2.3456 55.0044, -2.3718 54.9988, -2.3942 54.9955, -2.421 54.9911, -2.4481 54.9877, -2.4765 54.9839, -2.5048 54.9814, -2.5134 54.9875, -2.4897 54.9942)'), 18.6, null, 'Northumberland', array['Rollercoaster dips and blind summits hide oncoming traffic – overtake with great care; walkers crossing at Wall car parks; Housesteads and Steel Rigg car parks very busy in summer; sheep.', 'Medium confidence: the line or the source is partial (see the research notes). Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('ne-a68-carter-bar', 'drive', 'A68 to Carter Bar', 'From Otterburn up Redesdale past Catcleugh Reservoir and Byrness to the border viewpoint at Carter Bar. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(55.2319, -2.1809), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-2.1809 55.2319, -2.205 55.2395, -2.221 55.2516, -2.2409 55.263, -2.2612 55.2739, -2.285 55.283, -2.3079 55.292, -2.3349 55.2972, -2.3521 55.3091, -2.3735 55.3187, -2.3898 55.3221, -2.4171 55.3254, -2.4413 55.3333, -2.464 55.3421, -2.4777 55.3544)'), 15.7, null, 'Northumberland', array['Hidden dips and blind summits; military ranges (Otterburn) beside the road – obey red flags and don''t stop at range gates; snow closures at Carter Bar even in spring and autumn (Wikipedia); HGVs.']::text[]),
  ('ne-kielder', 'drive', 'Bellingham to Kielder', 'Up the North Tyne valley through Falstone and along the north shore of Kielder Water to Kielder village and castle. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(55.1445, -2.2549), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-2.2549 55.1445, -2.2785 55.1483, -2.2998 55.1574, -2.3258 55.165, -2.3481 55.1662, -2.3739 55.1663, -2.4008 55.1654, -2.4275 55.1687, -2.4502 55.1775, -2.4766 55.1726, -2.4978 55.1643, -2.5257 55.1661, -2.5393 55.1814, -2.5448 55.197, -2.563 55.2089, -2.5853 55.2185, -2.5799 55.234)'), 18.3, null, 'Northumberland', array['Remote with no fuel at Kielder – fill up in Bellingham; timber lorries; deer and red squirrels; the Kielder Forest Drive is a separate gravel toll road, not this route; dark skies park so no street lighting.']::text[]),
  ('ne-northumberland-coast', 'drive', 'Northumberland coast (B1339/B1340)', 'Coast-and-castles B-roads from Alnmouth through Longhoughton, Embleton, Beadnell and Seahouses to Bamburgh Castle. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(55.3929, -1.6366), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-1.6366 55.3929, -1.6264 55.4014, -1.6175 55.4157, -1.6166 55.4309, -1.6205 55.4364, -1.6222 55.4501, -1.6403 55.4613, -1.6446 55.4763, -1.64 55.491, -1.6385 55.5037, -1.6486 55.5184, -1.6604 55.5321, -1.6642 55.5463, -1.6452 55.5538, -1.6396 55.5554, -1.6438 55.5681, -1.6536 55.5815, -1.6705 55.5885, -1.6884 55.6004, -1.7141 55.6073)'), 21.4, null, 'Northumberland', array['Narrow in places with tractors and caravans; Seahouses and Bamburgh very busy in summer; village 30 mph limits; pay car parks.', 'Medium confidence: the line or the source is partial (see the research notes). Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('ne-a689-weardale', 'drive', 'A689 Weardale and Killhope', 'Up Weardale through St John''s Chapel and Cowshill, over Killhope Cross and down through Nenthead to Alston. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(54.7476, -2.0068), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-2.0068 54.7476, -2.0319 54.747, -2.0586 54.745, -2.0863 54.7419, -2.114 54.7376, -2.1415 54.738, -2.1674 54.7358, -2.1936 54.7405, -2.2161 54.7475, -2.2264 54.7609, -2.247 54.77, -2.2664 54.781, -2.2921 54.7841, -2.32 54.7842, -2.3439 54.7886, -2.365 54.7994, -2.3863 54.8082, -2.4136 54.8104, -2.441 54.8125)'), 20.3, null, 'North Pennines', array['Snow gates and frequent winter closures; mud and muck on the road; tight bend at Nenthead (BestBikingRoads); sheep; stop-start through the dale villages.']::text[]),
  ('ne-b6277-teesdale', 'drive', 'B6277 Teesdale and Yad Moss', 'Up Teesdale past Bowlees and High Force, then over the open moor at Yad Moss and down to Alston. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(54.6238, -2.083), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-2.083 54.6238, -2.1043 54.6297, -2.1265 54.639, -2.1483 54.648, -2.1754 54.6513, -2.1989 54.659, -2.2197 54.6698, -2.2383 54.6805, -2.2615 54.6892, -2.2771 54.7021, -2.2964 54.7122, -2.3202 54.7099, -2.3417 54.717, -2.3544 54.7307, -2.3667 54.7453, -2.3781 54.7596, -2.3913 54.7734, -2.4098 54.7817, -2.4246 54.794, -2.4343 54.8086, -2.441 54.8125)'), 21.9, null, 'North Pennines', array['Very bumpy beyond the last houses; suicidal sheep (BestBikingRoads); exposed and snow-prone over Yad Moss; cattle grids.']::text[]),
  ('ne-a166-garrowby', 'drive', 'A166 Garrowby Hill and the Wolds', 'East from Stamford Bridge up Garrowby Hill onto the Yorkshire Wolds, then over the top through Fridaythorpe and Wetwang to Driffield. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(53.9906, -0.9133), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-0.9133 53.9906, -0.8904 53.9976, -0.8643 53.9979, -0.8378 53.9976, -0.8105 53.9993, -0.7844 54.0001, -0.7562 54.0016, -0.7289 54.0004, -0.7036 54.0062, -0.6752 54.0138, -0.6522 54.0199, -0.6251 54.0198, -0.5968 54.0185, -0.5697 54.0207, -0.5422 54.0213, -0.514 54.0243, -0.49 54.0164, -0.4652 54.0098, -0.4414 54.0077, -0.4391 54.005)'), 20.8, null, 'Yorkshire Wolds', array['Steep climb and descent at Garrowby Hill; HGVs and tractors; poor surface near Driffield and queues behind lorries (BestBikingRoads).']::text[]),
  ('ne-b1225-wolds', 'drive', 'Caistor High Street (B1225)', 'The ridge-top "High Street" along the Lincolnshire Wolds from Caistor south past Belmont mast to the A158 near Horncastle. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(53.4969, -0.3155), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-0.3155 53.4969, -0.3008 53.4843, -0.296 53.4681, -0.2889 53.4528, -0.2753 53.4391, -0.2639 53.4256, -0.2395 53.4177, -0.231 53.4022, -0.2235 53.3859, -0.2064 53.3737, -0.1924 53.3603, -0.1799 53.3461, -0.1783 53.3306, -0.1737 53.3146, -0.1657 53.2992, -0.1624 53.2834, -0.1695 53.2685, -0.166 53.2535, -0.1617 53.2465)'), 19.7, null, 'Lincolnshire Wolds', array['Hidden crossroads on fast bends; mud from a motocross track near Belmont at weekends; popular with police including unmarked bikes (BestBikingRoads).']::text[]),
  ('ne-a5004-long-hill', 'drive', 'Long Hill (A5004)', 'From Buxton over Long Hill above the Goyt Valley and down to Whaley Bridge. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(53.2602, -1.92), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-1.92 53.2602, -1.9379 53.2699, -1.9507 53.2789, -1.9654 53.2828, -1.9741 53.2963, -1.9807 53.3104, -1.9851 53.3235, -1.9834 53.3302)'), 7.2, null, 'Peak District', array['A bend about halfway tightens sharply; deer can jump from the banks; cyclists; stone walls.']::text[]),
  ('ne-a54', 'drive', 'A54 Congleton to the Cat and Fiddle', 'From Congleton past Bosley and up through Wildboarclough country to meet the A537 near the Cat and Fiddle. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(53.1633, -2.2108), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-2.2108 53.1633, -2.1952 53.1717, -2.1744 53.1783, -2.162 53.1915, -2.1381 53.1952, -2.1167 53.1927, -2.0959 53.2004, -2.0741 53.2025, -2.051 53.1992, -2.0339 53.2048, -2.0114 53.2123, -1.9931 53.2225, -1.9738 53.234, -1.9504 53.2395)'), 14.5, null, 'Peak District', array['Average-speed cameras on the top section near the Cat and Fiddle; HGVs take the middle of the road on blind bends; sheep; roadworks – a section reopened in Oct 2026 with more work planned for spring 2027 (check before you go).', 'Medium confidence: the line or the source is partial (see the research notes). Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-ribblehead', 'photo', 'Ribblehead Viaduct', 'The 24-arch Settle–Carlisle railway viaduct under Whernside, at the B6255/B5479 junction. One of the classic Dales views; midway stop on the B6255.', private.pt(54.2059, -2.3609), null, null, null, 'Yorkshire Dales', array['Park only in the marked area by the junction or the station car park – not on the verges; very busy at weekends; the road beside the viaduct is narrow.', 'Medium confidence: the position is approximate or the details are not confirmed for 2026. Check before you go.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-buttertubs', 'photo', 'Buttertubs Pass summit', 'Lay-bys at the top of the Buttertubs road beside the 20 m limestone potholes. The Tour de France 2014 climb, with views down to Swaledale.', private.pt(54.3552, -2.2048), null, null, null, 'Yorkshire Dales', array['Small lay-bys only – pull fully off; unfenced drops; don''t block the narrow road.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-malham', 'photo', 'Malham (National Park Centre)', 'National Park car park in Malham village, the start of the walk to Malham Cove. Limestone cove and village scenery.', private.pt(54.0599, -2.1537), null, null, null, 'Yorkshire Dales', array['Pay car park that fills early in summer; narrow lanes into Malham – no roadside parking.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-cow-and-calf', 'photo', 'Cow and Calf, Ilkley Moor', 'Car park beside the Cow and Calf rocks above Ilkley, looking over Wharfedale. Famous gritstone rocks and a wide valley view.', private.pt(53.9165, -1.8001), null, null, null, 'West Yorkshire', array['Small car park, busy at weekends; inside the Bradford district vehicle-nuisance PSPO area – no meets, revving or stunts.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-chevin', 'photo', 'Surprise View, Otley Chevin', 'Surprise View car park on the Chevin above Otley, looking north over Wharfedale. Wide elevated view over the valley.', private.pt(53.8929, -1.6903), null, null, null, 'West Yorkshire', array['Small car park; local residents nearby – no gatherings; check closing times.', 'Medium confidence: the position is approximate or the details are not confirmed for 2026. Check before you go.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-hole-of-horcum', 'photo', 'Hole of Horcum (Saltergate)', 'National Park car park beside the A169 above the Hole of Horcum hollow. Big moorland bowl right on the A169 drive.', private.pt(54.332, -0.6906), null, null, null, 'North York Moors', array['Pay car park; the A169 is fast here – take care pulling in and out; busy at weekends.', 'Medium confidence: the position is approximate or the details are not confirmed for 2026. Check before you go.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-whitby-abbey', 'photo', 'Whitby Abbey headland', 'Abbey Headland car park next to the English Heritage abbey ruins above Whitby. Gothic ruins with the harbour below.', private.pt(54.4861, -0.6047), null, null, null, 'North York Moors', array['Pay car park; Whitby is very busy in summer and during Goth Weekends; narrow streets in the old town.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-roseberry', 'photo', 'Roseberry Topping (Gribdale Gate)', 'Gribdale Gate picnic site and car park on the moor edge between Roseberry Topping and Captain Cook''s Monument. National Trust hill with a distinctive half-cone summit.', private.pt(54.4908, -1.0874), null, null, null, 'North York Moors', array['Narrow, steep lane from Great Ayton; small car park; walkers.', 'Medium confidence: the position is approximate or the details are not confirmed for 2026. Check before you go.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-saltburn', 'photo', 'Saltburn Pier', 'Victorian pier and cliff lift with lower-promenade parking. The last pleasure pier in Yorkshire, with the cliff tramway behind.', private.pt(54.5869, -0.9703), null, null, null, 'Teesside', array['Pay parking; steep access road; busy summer weekends.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-flamborough', 'photo', 'Flamborough Head lighthouse', 'Car park at the lighthouse on the chalk headland. White cliffs, sea stacks and the lighthouse.', private.pt(54.1162, -0.0834), null, null, null, 'Yorkshire Wolds', array['Pay car park; exposed in bad weather; keep back from cliff edges.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-humber-bridge', 'photo', 'Humber Bridge viewing area', 'Viewing area and car park at the south (Barton) end of the Humber Bridge. Big suspension-bridge backdrop.', private.pt(53.6969, -0.4448), null, null, null, 'Lincolnshire', array['Check car park hours; no gatherings.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-surprise-view', 'photo', 'Surprise View, Hathersage', 'National Trust car park on the A6187 above Hathersage, looking across the Hope Valley. One of the best-known Peak District viewpoints, by Millstone Edge.', private.pt(53.3172, -1.6231), null, null, null, 'Peak District', array['Pay car park (NT members free); busy at weekends; the A6187 bend here is fast.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-stanage', 'photo', 'Stanage Edge (Hook''s Car)', 'Hook''s Car car park below Stanage Edge, north of Hathersage. Long gritstone edge with views over the Hope Valley.', private.pt(53.3429, -1.6342), null, null, null, 'Peak District', array['Pay car park; narrow lanes; climbers and walkers.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-ashness-bridge', 'photo', 'Ashness Bridge', 'Packhorse bridge on the Watendlath road above Derwentwater, with the classic view to Skiddaw. One of the most photographed views in the Lake District.', private.pt(54.5672, -3.13), null, null, null, 'Lake District', array['Single-track road off the B5289 with few passing places; tiny car park just above the bridge – don''t block the road or bridge.', 'Medium confidence: the position is approximate or the details are not confirmed for 2026. Check before you go.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-honister', 'photo', 'Honister Slate Mine', 'Car park at the slate mine on the summit of Honister Pass. Top of the Honister drive with views down both valleys.', private.pt(54.5112, -3.1992), null, null, null, 'Lake District', array['Pay car park; busy with visitors and walkers.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-castlerigg', 'photo', 'Castlerigg Stone Circle', 'Neolithic stone circle above Keswick with roadside lay-by parking. Stones with a ring of fells behind.', private.pt(54.6029, -3.0984), null, null, null, 'Lake District', array['Narrow lane – park only in the lay-by; no vehicles on the grass; English Heritage site.', 'Medium confidence: the position is approximate or the details are not confirmed for 2026. Check before you go.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-wasdale', 'photo', 'Wast Water (Overbeck Bridge)', 'National Trust car park at Overbeck Bridge on the Wast Water shore road, facing the screes and Great Gable. Wast Water is England''s deepest lake; a famous mountain view.', private.pt(54.4497, -3.285), null, null, null, 'Lake District', array['Remote, narrow dead-end valley road with no fuel; small pay car park; sheep.', 'Medium confidence: the position is approximate or the details are not confirmed for 2026. Check before you go.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-jubilee-tower', 'photo', 'Jubilee Tower, Quernmore', 'Car park by the Jubilee Tower on the Trough of Bowland road above Lancaster, looking out to Morecambe Bay. Viewpoint at the western end of the Trough of Bowland drive.', private.pt(54.0102, -2.7001), null, null, null, 'Lancashire', array['Small car park on an unfenced moor road; sheep; no gatherings.', 'Medium confidence: the position is approximate or the details are not confirmed for 2026. Check before you go.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-high-force', 'photo', 'High Force', 'Waterfall car park opposite the High Force Hotel on the B6277. One of England''s biggest waterfalls, on the Teesdale drive.', private.pt(54.652, -2.18), null, null, null, 'North Pennines', array['Pay car park and a charge for the waterfall path; B6277 traffic.', 'Medium confidence: the position is approximate or the details are not confirmed for 2026. Check before you go.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-steel-rigg', 'photo', 'Steel Rigg (Hadrian''s Wall)', 'National Park car park just off the Military Road near The Sill, below the Whin Sill crags. The best-known stretch of Hadrian''s Wall; the former Sycamore Gap tree (felled in 2023) is a short walk east.', private.pt(55.003, -2.3908), null, null, null, 'Northumberland', array['Pay car park; very busy in summer; narrow access lane.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-kielder-castle', 'photo', 'Kielder Castle', 'Forest centre and car park at Kielder Castle, the end of the Kielder drive. Forest, reservoir and dark-sky park.', private.pt(55.2339, -2.5801), null, null, null, 'Northumberland', array['Pay car park; remote with no fuel; check opening times.', 'Medium confidence: the position is approximate or the details are not confirmed for 2026. Check before you go.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-bamburgh', 'photo', 'Bamburgh Castle', 'The Links car park in the dunes below Bamburgh Castle. Castle on its rock above the beach; end of the coast drive.', private.pt(55.6043, -1.6972), null, null, null, 'Northumberland', array['Pay parking; very busy in summer; no driving on the dunes or beach.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-craster', 'photo', 'Craster (for Dunstanburgh Castle)', 'Quarry car park in Craster, at the start of the coast path to Dunstanburgh Castle. Harbour village with the castle ruin along the coast.', private.pt(55.4709, -1.5958), null, null, null, 'Northumberland', array['Pay car park; village lanes are narrow – no driving down to the harbour.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-lindisfarne', 'photo', 'Holy Island (Lindisfarne)', 'Chare Ends car park on Holy Island, reached over the tidal causeway. Causeway, priory and castle.', private.pt(55.675, -1.8005), null, null, null, 'Northumberland', array['The causeway floods at high tide – check the council''s safe crossing times before you go and never cross outside them; pay parking.']::text[]),
  ('ne-p-angel', 'photo', 'Angel of the North', 'Antony Gormley''s 20 m steel sculpture in Gateshead, with a small free car park beside it. The North East''s best-known landmark.', private.pt(54.9141, -1.5895), null, null, null, 'Tyne and Wear', array['Small car park off the A167 – short stops only, no meets.']::text[]),
  ('sws-b3212-dartmoor', 'drive', 'B3212 across Dartmoor', 'The main road over the high moor: Yelverton, Princetown, Two Bridges, Postbridge and the Warren House Inn, then down into Moretonhampstead. BestBikingRoads (Yelverton–Exeter): the moorland section is open, consistent and fast with big views; Motorcycle Sport & Leisure calls the stretch past Princetown one of the best roads in the country. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(50.4933, -4.0798), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-4.0798 50.4933, -4.065 50.5013, -4.0461 50.5089, -4.0322 50.5196, -4.0176 50.5297, -4.0015 50.5392, -3.9867 50.5491, -3.9691 50.5573, -3.9521 50.5642, -3.9358 50.5739, -3.9229 50.5855, -3.9079 50.5962, -3.8913 50.606, -3.8732 50.6145, -3.8734 50.6167, -3.8591 50.6255, -3.8437 50.6347, -3.8284 50.6415, -3.8117 50.6484, -3.7922 50.6547, -3.7736 50.6598, -3.765 50.6611)'), 20.4, null, 'South West', array['Dartmoor 40 mph limit on the open moor. Ponies, sheep and cattle roam free and are hit often – Visit Dartmoor singles out the open common between Peek Hill and Princetown. Cattle grids; mud and gravel on bends after Moretonhampstead; slow tourist traffic; fog and snow on the tops.']::text[]),
  ('sws-b3357-dartmeet', 'drive', 'B3357 Tavistock to Ashburton via Dartmeet', 'West to east across Dartmoor via Merrivale and Two Bridges, down the steep hill to Dartmeet, then Poundsgate and Holne Bridge to Ashburton. Rated on BestBikingRoads as part of the "Dartmoor Treat" (Roborough–Two Bridges–Ponsworthy) and Tavistock–Moretonhampstead rides. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(50.5489, -4.1431), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-4.1431 50.5489, -4.1236 50.5526, -4.1009 50.5521, -4.0817 50.559, -4.0599 50.5566, -4.0396 50.557, -4.0174 50.5568, -3.9948 50.5574, -3.9723 50.5583, -3.9509 50.5563, -3.9288 50.5574, -3.9078 50.5534, -3.889 50.5456, -3.8697 50.5446, -3.8498 50.5449, -3.8305 50.5392, -3.8238 50.527, -3.8101 50.5228, -3.7903 50.5216, -3.7735 50.5131, -3.7549 50.5118, -3.7559 50.5161)'), 20.5, null, 'South West', array['Dartmoor 40 mph limit; free-roaming livestock and cattle grids. The Dartmeet hill and the road on to Poundsgate are narrow with tight bends – very slow in summer, and Dartmeet car parks fill up.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sws-a39-exmoor', 'drive', 'A39 Exmoor coast: Porlock and Countisbury hills', 'Out of Minehead to Porlock, up Porlock Hill onto the open moor past County Gate, then down Countisbury Hill into Lynmouth. Adventure Bike Rider and RideTo both pick the A39 Porlock–Lynmouth stretch as one of the best roads in the South West: hairpins, sweeping moorland bends and sea views. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.201, -3.48), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-3.48 51.201, -3.4996 51.2008, -3.5225 51.2024, -3.5452 51.2012, -3.5651 51.208, -3.5842 51.2082, -3.6021 51.2066, -3.6194 51.2026, -3.642 51.2043, -3.664 51.2047, -3.6818 51.2128, -3.7037 51.217, -3.7247 51.2217, -3.7425 51.2259, -3.7643 51.229, -3.7849 51.2294, -3.8057 51.2303, -3.829 51.23)'), 17.1, null, 'South West', array['Porlock Hill is about 1 in 4 (25%) with two hairpins – use a low gear down; caravans and long vehicles struggle (the Porlock Scenic Toll Road is the gentler, paid alternative). Countisbury Hill is also very steep. Sheep and Exmoor ponies on the open moor; summer caravans and coaches; fog on the tops.']::text[]),
  ('sws-b3306-penwith', 'drive', 'B3306 West Cornwall coast road', 'Hugs the Penwith coast past Zennor, Morvah, Pendeen and Botallack, with the Atlantic on one side and moorland on the other. Wikipedia: "often considered one of the greatest driving roads in the United Kingdom" for its scenery. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(50.2059, -5.4898), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-5.4898 50.2059, -5.5097 50.2046, -5.5275 50.1979, -5.5424 50.1961, -5.562 50.1936, -5.575 50.1837, -5.5917 50.1818, -5.6066 50.1747, -5.6243 50.1675, -5.6315 50.1597, -5.6436 50.1549, -5.6636 50.1519, -5.6755 50.1409, -5.6842 50.1328, -5.681 50.1243)'), 13.8, null, 'South West', array['Narrow and twisting between granite walls with blind bends; tractors, cyclists and coaches in summer; St Ives streets are very congested; flood damage has closed it near Zennor before.']::text[]),
  ('sws-b3157-jurassic', 'drive', 'B3157 Jurassic Coast road', 'Burton Bradstock, the climb over Abbotsbury Hill with views along Chesil Beach, then Portesham and Chickerell into Weymouth. BestBikingRoads rates the scenery 4.6/5 and the corners highly: good bends with clear exits and views over Lyme Bay and Chesil Beach. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(50.7209, -2.7467), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-2.7467 50.7209, -2.7563 50.7193, -2.7418 50.7091, -2.7271 50.701, -2.7075 50.6951, -2.6849 50.693, -2.6659 50.6873, -2.6467 50.6801, -2.6264 50.6739, -2.6094 50.6658, -2.5879 50.6641, -2.569 50.6674, -2.5511 50.6629, -2.5382 50.6512, -2.5307 50.6377, -2.5144 50.6278, -2.5011 50.6172, -2.4822 50.6187, -2.4698 50.6228)'), 17.8, null, 'South West', array['Blind crests and crossroads; mostly 50 mph; reviewers report mobile speed cameras and police at weekends; holiday traffic and walkers; morning fog.']::text[]),
  ('sws-b3081-zigzag', 'drive', 'B3081 Zig Zag Hill and Cranborne Chase', 'Climbs out of Shaftesbury up the hairpins of Zig Zag Hill, crosses Cranborne Chase via Tollard Royal and Sixpenny Handley, then Verwood to the A31 near Ringwood. BestBikingRoads (Shaftesbury–Ringwood) highlights Zig Zag Hill, the Cranborne Chase landscape and Tollard Royal; Total 911 lists Zig Zag Hill as a great road. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.0045, -2.188), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-2.188 51.0045, -2.1743 50.9948, -2.159 50.9864, -2.1433 50.9856, -2.1231 50.9811, -2.1197 50.9685, -2.104 50.9611, -2.0824 50.9595, -2.0669 50.9508, -2.0472 50.9549, -2.0249 50.9561, -2.0044 50.9518, -1.9852 50.9488, -1.97 50.94, -1.9543 50.9295, -1.9434 50.9173, -1.9361 50.9083, -1.9358 50.8972, -1.9198 50.8893, -1.8993 50.8845, -1.8777 50.8814, -1.8576 50.8752, -1.8402 50.866, -1.824 50.8558, -1.8083 50.8456, -1.8055 50.8441)'), 24.2, null, 'South West', array['Zig Zag Hill hairpins are steep, narrow and greasy with leaves, and downhill traffic drifts across; gravel at the top; Tollard Royal is slow; police reported on the Sixpenny Handley–Cranborne straight; horses and farm traffic. Dorset Council closes the hill for resurfacing at times.']::text[]),
  ('sws-a32-meon', 'drive', 'A32 Meon Valley', 'Fast A-road north through the Meon Valley in the South Downs: Droxford, Exton, West Meon (Loomies café) and on towards Alton. BestBikingRoads (A32 Fareham–Chawton): a fast A-road through a few villages, with Loomies café and fuel halfway. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(50.922, -1.1619), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-1.1619 50.922, -1.1462 50.9317, -1.1414 50.945, -1.1387 50.9593, -1.1315 50.9721, -1.1247 50.9839, -1.1181 50.9975, -1.1051 51.007, -1.0862 51.0132, -1.0768 51.0262, -1.0681 51.0393, -1.0503 51.0481, -1.0342 51.0583, -1.0189 51.069, -1.0042 51.0798, -0.997 51.093, -0.9938 51.1071, -0.9942 51.1212, -0.9932 51.1323, -0.99 51.1286)'), 18.5, null, 'South of England', array['Popular with bikers, so police patrol at weekends; Warnford Parish Council asks residents to report noisy bikes; 30/40 mph through Droxford, Warnford and West Meon; farm traffic.']::text[]),
  ('sws-a272-downs', 'drive', 'A272 Winchester to Petworth', 'Over the downs past Cheesefoot Head and West Meon Hut to Petersfield, then on through Rogate and Midhurst to Petworth. BestBikingRoads (Winchester–Petersfield): long sweeping bends and downland views; PistonHeads "Surrey back roads medley" praises the sweeping A272 and its walled villages. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.0558, -1.2588), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-1.2588 51.0558, -1.2449 51.0454, -1.2241 51.04, -1.2034 51.0388, -1.1812 51.0421, -1.1606 51.0469, -1.1384 51.0502, -1.1175 51.0451, -1.0979 51.038, -1.0787 51.031, -1.0559 51.0306, -1.0341 51.0309, -1.0215 51.0197, -1.0033 51.013, -0.9845 51.0093, -0.9622 51.008, -0.941 51.0071, -0.9283 51.0097, -0.9098 51.0149, -0.8914 51.0078, -0.8691 51.0067, -0.848 51.0082, -0.8286 51.003, -0.8113 50.9961, -0.7904 50.9937, -0.7693 50.9888, -0.7466 50.9878, -0.7343 50.9911, -0.7169 50.9921, -0.6957 50.9894, -0.6738 50.9895, -0.6516 50.987, -0.629 50.988, -0.611 50.9868)'), 33.1, null, 'South of England', array['Frequent police patrols, especially weekends and Wednesday evenings; 40 mph limits; loose stones at the West Meon Hut crossroads; town traffic in Petersfield and Midhurst; narrow streets in Petworth.']::text[]),
  ('sws-new-forest', 'drive', 'New Forest: Rhinefield and Bolderwood', 'Rhinefield Road and the Rhinefield Ornamental Drive under giant redwoods and Douglas firs, a short A35 link, then Bolderwood Road across the open forest to Bolderwood. Forestry England: Bolderwood is the most visited car park in the New Forest; the ornamental drives are lined with some of the tallest trees in Britain. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(50.8192, -1.5771), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-1.5771 50.8192, -1.5961 50.8226, -1.6171 50.8241, -1.6242 50.8362, -1.6226 50.8497, -1.6102 50.858, -1.5928 50.8667, -1.5992 50.8731, -1.6209 50.8691, -1.6434 50.8691, -1.6584 50.8787, -1.6564 50.8767)'), 10.2, null, 'South of England', array['40 mph limit across the unfenced forest – ponies, donkeys, cattle and deer roam and are killed on the roads every year; cattle grids; narrow drives busy with cyclists and walkers in summer; never park on verges – use the Forestry England car parks.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sws-b4632-cleeve', 'drive', 'B4632 Broadway to Cheltenham over Cleeve Hill', 'Along the foot of the Cotswold edge to Winchcombe, then up over Cleeve Hill – the highest point of the Cotswolds – and down into Cheltenham. Used in Bike magazine''s Cotswolds route (with the B4077); Cleeve Hill sits beside the B4632. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.0361, -1.86), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-1.86 52.0361, -1.8801 52.0339, -1.8954 52.0237, -1.9097 52.0125, -1.9247 52.002, -1.9319 51.9887, -1.9391 51.9754, -1.9555 51.9662, -1.965 51.9544, -1.9813 51.9467, -2.0025 51.949, -2.0215 51.9421, -2.0386 51.9332, -2.0396 51.919, -2.0527 51.9114, -2.0642 51.9092)'), 14.9, null, 'South West', array['Winchcombe high street is narrow; Cleeve Hill has steep, tight bends and a common with walkers and livestock; Prescott Hill Climb is just off this road – event-day traffic; Cheltenham town traffic at the end.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sws-b4077-stanway', 'drive', 'B4077 Stow to Toddington (Stanway Hill)', 'West from Stow across the high wolds past Ford, then down the long Stanway Hill towards Toddington. Used in Bike magazine''s Cotswolds route (with the B4632); the Stanway Hill descent is the highlight. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.93, -1.7248), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-1.7248 51.93, -1.7305 51.9436, -1.7494 51.9493, -1.7724 51.95, -1.7935 51.9492, -1.8153 51.9542, -1.8385 51.9563, -1.8611 51.9594, -1.8808 51.9646, -1.8928 51.9764, -1.9042 51.9869, -1.9267 51.99, -1.9497 51.9906)'), 12, null, 'South West', array['Stanway Hill is steep with a sharp bend at the bottom and HGVs; racehorses ridden near Ford; mud from farms.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sws-lambourn-loop', 'drive', 'Lambourn Loop (Berkshire Downs)', 'Up the A338 to Wantage, west on the B4507, south over the downs on the B4001 to Lambourn, and back on the Newbury road. PistonHeads "My Dream Drive": fast, flowing A338 with good sight lines (no hedges between Great Shefford and Wantage), then rough, testing B-roads and views over Oxfordshire. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.4745, -1.4492), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-1.4492 51.4745, -1.4376 51.4854, -1.429 51.4985, -1.4251 51.5125, -1.4224 51.5258, -1.4245 51.5397, -1.431 51.5536, -1.4285 51.5673, -1.428 51.5815, -1.4408 51.5865, -1.4636 51.5838, -1.4808 51.5778, -1.4935 51.5681, -1.5095 51.5587, -1.5183 51.5453, -1.5227 51.5311, -1.523 51.5168, -1.5219 51.504, -1.5052 51.4948, -1.4857 51.4893, -1.4694 51.4803, -1.4492 51.4745)'), 21, null, 'South of England', array['A338 is 50 mph with a sharp left-hander at the bottom of a crest halfway along; racehorses ridden on and crossing the roads around Lambourn; broken, uneven surfaces on the B4001; the Lambourn–Shefford road is busier.']::text[]),
  ('sws-b2110-turners-hill', 'drive', 'Turner''s Hill Road (B2110)', 'Through Turner''s Hill and past Worth Abbey, then High Beeches Lane through woodland to Handcross and on to the A281. PistonHeads "My Dream Drive": low hedges and open views alternate with twisting woodland sections that need precision. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.124, -0.011), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-0.011 51.124, -0.0285 51.117, -0.0445 51.1072, -0.0637 51.1075, -0.0856 51.1034, -0.1067 51.0985, -0.1269 51.0926, -0.1374 51.0815, -0.1567 51.074, -0.172 51.064, -0.1936 51.06, -0.2096 51.0511, -0.2299 51.0446, -0.2491 51.0369, -0.2625 51.0331)'), 13.7, null, 'South of England', array['Woodland sections twist and are often damp; Handcross village; the A281 is busy. Mid Sussex car-cruising PSPO covers the Birches Industrial Estate in East Grinstead near the start.']::text[]),
  ('sws-beachy-head', 'drive', 'Beachy Head Road', 'Up from Eastbourne to Beachy Head, then along the clifftop road to Birling Gap and down to East Dean. PistonHeads "My Dream Drive" and BestBikingRoads: hairpins under the trees, then a clifftop road with huge sea views. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(50.759, 0.269), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(0.269 50.759, 0.2537 50.7536, 0.252 50.7399, 0.2333 50.7393, 0.2135 50.7407, 0.2055 50.7467, 0.2075 50.7576)'), 5.9, null, 'South of England', array['Bumpy, potholed surface reported towards Birling Gap; strong crosswinds; walkers crossing to the cliffs; busy at weekends. Park only in the marked car parks.']::text[]),
  ('sws-a285-duncton', 'drive', 'A285 Petworth to Chichester (Duncton Hill)', 'South from Petworth through Duncton, up the wooded climb of Duncton Hill onto the South Downs, then past Upwaltham and Halnaker to Chichester. BestBikingRoads (Surrey/West Sussex loop): the single-carriageway A285 south towards Chichester was the reviewer''s highlight. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(50.9861, -0.609), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-0.609 50.9861, -0.6138 50.9735, -0.6242 50.9613, -0.6332 50.9482, -0.6361 50.9376, -0.6419 50.9269, -0.6575 50.9167, -0.6653 50.9043, -0.6712 50.8907, -0.6823 50.8786, -0.6995 50.8705, -0.7182 50.8622, -0.7305 50.8522, -0.7487 50.8439, -0.7553 50.8422)'), 13.4, null, 'South of England', array['Bumpy surfaces in parts; Duncton Hill is steep with tight bends under trees, slippery when wet; Goodwood event days bring heavy traffic near Halnaker; ends on the busy A27.']::text[]),
  ('sws-surrey-hills', 'drive', 'Surrey Hills lanes: Cranleigh to Newlands Corner', 'The B2127 to Ewhurst, then narrow lanes over Pitch Hill and through Peaslake to Shere, finishing on the A25 at Newlands Corner. PistonHeads "Surrey back roads medley": rocky cuttings on the north–south Surrey Hills roads and the Newlands Corner viewpoint. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.1409, -0.4881), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-0.4881 51.1409, -0.4682 51.1458, -0.4465 51.1473, -0.444 51.1578, -0.4452 51.1713, -0.4436 51.1842, -0.4433 51.1977, -0.4517 51.2081, -0.4655 51.2171, -0.4792 51.2244, -0.4988 51.2312, -0.5068 51.2328)'), 10.4, null, 'South of England', array['Narrow, sunken lanes full of cyclists and walkers at weekends; Shere and Peaslake are slow villages; Newlands Corner car park is camera-enforced pay parking and police treat it (with Box Hill) as an anti-social driving hotspot – don''t gather there.', 'Medium confidence: the place or line was rebuilt from a postcode or village names. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-bedruthan', 'photo', 'Bedruthan Steps (Carnewas)', 'Clifftop car park above the rock stacks of Bedruthan beach on the north Cornish coast. One of Cornwall''s best-known coastal views.', private.pt(50.4853, -5.0327), null, null, null, 'South West', array['Pay car park; cliff edges unfenced; busy in summer.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-botallack', 'photo', 'Botallack mine engine houses', 'National Trust car park by the Count House above the clifftop mine engine houses, just off the B3306. Famous Crown Mines backdrop at the end of the Penwith coast road.', private.pt(50.1408, -5.6891), null, null, null, 'South West', array['NT car park charges; narrow lane from the B3306; don''t drive on the mine tracks.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-lizard-point', 'photo', 'Lizard Point', 'Car park at the most southerly point of mainland Britain, by the lighthouse and cafés. Unique "most southerly" landmark.', private.pt(49.9594, -5.2064), null, null, null, 'South West', array['Narrow road through Lizard village; small car parks fill in summer.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-burrator', 'photo', 'Burrator Reservoir', 'Free roadside parking areas by the dam, with Sheeps Tor behind the water. Classic Dartmoor reservoir view near Yelverton (start of the B3212 drive).', private.pt(50.4942, -4.0447), null, null, null, 'South West', array['Narrow lanes; park only in the marked areas; ponies and sheep.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-dartmeet', 'photo', 'Dartmeet', 'Free car park where the East and West Dart rivers meet, beside the old clapper bridge. On the B3357 drive; river and moorland backdrop.', private.pt(50.5443, -3.875), null, null, null, 'South West', array['Steep, narrow hill either side; very busy summer weekends; free-roaming livestock.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-valley-of-rocks', 'photo', 'Valley of Rocks, Lynton', 'Pay-and-display car park in the dry valley of rock towers west of Lynton, with feral goats. Dramatic Exmoor coastal scenery near the end of the A39 drive.', private.pt(51.2325, -3.8518), null, null, null, 'South West', array['Narrow road with a toll section beyond; goats on the road.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-county-gate', 'photo', 'County Gate, Exmoor', 'Car park on the A39 at the Devon–Somerset border, looking over the East Lyn valley and the sea. Natural stop on the A39 Exmoor coast drive.', private.pt(51.2241, -3.7296), null, null, null, 'South West', array['Turn in carefully from the A39; exposed and foggy in poor weather.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-dunkery', 'photo', 'Dunkery Beacon', 'Moorland car park below Exmoor''s highest point. Big views over Exmoor towards the Bristol Channel.', private.pt(51.1541, -3.5803), null, null, null, 'South West', array['Unfenced moor roads, sheep and ponies; single-track sections. Car park position is an unnamed OSM car park south of the summit.', 'Medium confidence: car park position is an unnamed OSM car park near the summit. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-portland-bill', 'photo', 'Portland Bill', 'Pay car park by the red-and-white lighthouse at the southern tip of Portland. Lighthouse and rough-sea backdrop.', private.pt(50.5156, -2.4565), null, null, null, 'South West', array['Pay parking; very windy; busy summer weekends.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-durdle-door', 'photo', 'Durdle Door', 'Estate pay car park at the top of the path to the limestone arch. One of the most photographed spots on the Jurassic Coast.', private.pt(50.6241, -2.2693), null, null, null, 'South West', array['Private estate car park with fees; very busy in summer; no gatherings.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-corfe', 'photo', 'Corfe Castle', 'Pay car park on the A351 below the castle ruins. Castle ruin on its hill in the Purbeck gap.', private.pt(50.6451, -2.0603), null, null, null, 'South West', array['A351 is busy and slow in summer; car park charges.', 'Medium confidence: car park position is an unnamed OSM car park near the castle. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-abbotsbury-hill', 'photo', 'Abbotsbury Hill viewpoint', 'Free car park and viewpoint on the B3157 above Abbotsbury, looking along Chesil Beach. On the B3157 Jurassic Coast drive.', private.pt(50.6705, -2.6201), null, null, null, 'South West', array['Pull in slowly – fast road with crests; exposed.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-westbury-white-horse', 'photo', 'Westbury White Horse', 'Free car park on Bratton Downs by the chalk horse and Iron Age fort. Views over the Vale of Pewsey and the white horse.', private.pt(51.2614, -2.1453), null, null, null, 'South West', array['Single-track lane up; livestock; no gatherings.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-broadway-tower', 'photo', 'Broadway Tower', 'Car park by the 18th-century folly tower on the Cotswold edge (just over the Worcestershire line). Classic Cotswolds landmark near the start of the B4632 drive.', private.pt(52.0236, -1.8388), null, null, null, 'South West', array['Paid parking for the country park; opening times apply.', 'Medium confidence: car park position is an unnamed OSM car park near the tower. Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-butser', 'photo', 'Butser Hill', 'Hampshire County Council pay car park on the top of Butser Hill (Queen Elizabeth Country Park). Highest point of the South Downs, views to the Isle of Wight.', private.pt(50.9759, -0.9862), null, null, null, 'South of England', array['Pay parking; gates close in the evening; A3 access is fast.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-bolderwood', 'photo', 'Bolderwood, New Forest', 'Forestry England car park at the end of the New Forest drive, with deer viewing platform nearby. Most-visited car park in the New Forest.', private.pt(50.8768, -1.6564), null, null, null, 'South of England', array['40 mph forest roads with roaming animals; car park can be very busy.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-needles', 'photo', 'The Needles (Alum Bay)', 'Pay car park at the Needles Landmark Attraction above Alum Bay. Chalk stacks and lighthouse at the western tip of the Isle of Wight.', private.pt(50.6672, -1.567), null, null, null, 'South of England', array['Ferry needed to reach the island; pay parking; busy in summer.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-walbury-hill', 'photo', 'Walbury Hill and Combe Gibbet', 'Free car park on the ridge road beside Walbury Hill, the highest chalk hill in south-east England. Big downland views; Combe Gibbet along the ridge.', private.pt(51.3521, -1.4558), null, null, null, 'South of England', array['Narrow, steep lanes up; livestock; exposed in bad weather.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-uffington', 'photo', 'Uffington White Horse', 'National Trust pay car park below White Horse Hill. Bronze Age chalk horse and Dragon Hill; near the Lambourn Loop.', private.pt(51.5773, -1.5784), null, null, null, 'South of England', array['NT car park charges; narrow lane; no gatherings.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-devils-punch-bowl', 'photo', 'Devil''s Punch Bowl, Hindhead', 'National Trust car park and café beside the old A3 route above the Punch Bowl. Classic Surrey Hills viewpoint.', private.pt(51.1142, -0.7288), null, null, null, 'South of England', array['NT car park charges; busy at weekends.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-devils-dyke', 'photo', 'Devil''s Dyke', 'National Trust car park at the top of the dry valley north of Brighton. Panoramic South Downs view.', private.pt(50.8856, -0.2119), null, null, null, 'South of England', array['NT car park charges; busy at weekends; Brighton side roads are residential.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-ditchling-beacon', 'photo', 'Ditchling Beacon', 'National Trust car park on the summit of Ditchling Beacon. One of the highest points on the South Downs.', private.pt(50.9009, -0.1051), null, null, null, 'South of England', array['Ditchling Road up the hill is narrow and steep with many cyclists; NT charges.']::text[]),
  ('sws-p-birling-gap', 'photo', 'Birling Gap and the Seven Sisters', 'National Trust car park by the visitor centre, looking along the Seven Sisters cliffs. On the Beachy Head Road drive.', private.pt(50.743, 0.2016), null, null, null, 'South of England', array['NT car park charges; cliff edges eroding – keep back.']::text[]),
  ('mw-bwlch-y-groes', 'drive', 'Bwlch y Groes (Dinas Mawddwy to Llanuwchllyn)', 'Up the Dyfi valley through Llanymawddwy, over Bwlch y Groes (545 m) past the cross at the top, then down Cwm Cynllwyd to Llanuwchllyn near Bala Lake. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.7217, -3.6887), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-3.6887 52.7217, -3.6663 52.7287, -3.6453 52.7381, -3.634 52.7524, -3.6239 52.7642, -3.6224 52.7783, -3.6117 52.7922, -3.6123 52.8065, -3.6237 52.8208, -3.6449 52.8309, -3.6582 52.8439, -3.6671 52.8544, -3.6747 52.8615)'), 13.1, null, 'Eryri (Snowdonia)', array['Mostly single-track with passing places; the southern climb is about 1.7 mi with gradients up to 1 in 4 and a double hairpin; farm dogs and sheep; cyclists; exposed and best left alone in snow, ice or fog.']::text[]),
  ('mw-elan-mountain-road', 'drive', 'Elan Valley mountain road (Rhayader to Devil''s Bridge)', 'West out of Rhayader on the mountain road above the Elan Valley reservoirs to Pont ar Elan, across the open Cambrian Mountains to Cwmystwyth, then the B4574 to Devil''s Bridge. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.3018, -3.5122), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-3.5122 52.3018, -3.5292 52.3042, -3.5493 52.3141, -3.5744 52.318, -3.5895 52.3302, -3.6128 52.3336, -3.6365 52.3406, -3.6574 52.35, -3.6727 52.3623, -3.6918 52.3665, -3.7163 52.3621, -3.7376 52.3602, -3.7617 52.3549, -3.7826 52.3518, -3.7995 52.3595, -3.8217 52.3655, -3.845 52.3717, -3.849 52.3773)'), 18.4, null, 'Mid Wales', array['Unfenced moorland with sheep on the road; narrow sections and cattle grids; no fuel between Rhayader and Devil''s Bridge; exposed in bad weather.']::text[]),
  ('mw-gospel-pass', 'drive', 'Gospel Pass (Hay-on-Wye to Llanthony)', 'South from Hay-on-Wye up to the Gospel Pass between Twmpa and Hay Bluff, then down the Vale of Ewyas past Capel-y-ffin to Llanthony Priory. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.0744, -3.1258), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-3.1258 52.0744, -3.1184 52.0648, -3.1045 52.0525, -3.1061 52.0421, -3.1105 52.0265, -3.1157 52.0111, -3.1018 51.9976, -3.0877 51.9844, -3.0819 51.9731, -3.0628 51.9631, -3.0521 51.95, -3.0365 51.9445)'), 12.2, null, 'Bannau Brycheiniog (Brecon Beacons)', array['Single-track over most of its length with passing places – expect to reverse; free-roaming ponies and sheep; walkers parking near the top; occasionally blocked by snow.', 'Medium confidence: the line or the source is partial (see the research notes). Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('mw-a470-beacons', 'drive', 'A470 over the Beacons (Merthyr to Libanus)', 'North from the Heads of the Valleys road past the Taf Fawr reservoirs, over the pass at Storey Arms below Pen y Fan, and down to Libanus near Brecon. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.7607, -3.4126), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-3.4126 51.7607, -3.4196 51.7765, -3.4296 51.7913, -3.4407 51.8051, -3.4446 51.8204, -3.4602 51.8336, -3.4665 51.8491, -3.4714 51.8656, -3.4838 51.8728, -3.4941 51.8839, -3.4898 51.901, -3.4723 51.913, -3.4605 51.9224)'), 13.4, null, 'Bannau Brycheiniog (Brecon Beacons)', array['Heavy weekend traffic and caravans; marked and unmarked police bikes on busy days (BestBikingRoads); Pen y Fan walkers parking at Pont ar Daf and Storey Arms; snow on the pass.']::text[]),
  ('mw-a44-pumlumon', 'drive', 'A44 Llangurig to Aberystwyth', 'West from Llangurig up the Wye valley and over the shoulder of Pumlumon at Eisteddfa Gurig, down through Ponterwyd and on towards Aberystwyth. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.406, -3.6049), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-3.6049 52.406, -3.6296 52.4103, -3.6534 52.4157, -3.6772 52.4226, -3.704 52.4295, -3.7289 52.4261, -3.75 52.4348, -3.7717 52.4405, -3.7823 52.4309, -3.7978 52.4212, -3.8215 52.4164, -3.8407 52.4122, -3.8618 52.4098, -3.8857 52.4145, -3.9044 52.41, -3.9223 52.412, -3.9456 52.407, -3.9707 52.4033, -3.9821 52.4044)'), 19.7, null, 'Mid Wales', array['Holiday traffic at weekends – ride it midweek; police in Capel Bangor (BestBikingRoads); sheep; exposed over the top.']::text[]),
  ('mw-a483-llandovery-builth', 'drive', 'A483 Llandovery to Builth Wells', 'North-east from Llandovery over the Sugar Loaf pass to Llanwrtyd Wells, then through Beulah and down the Irfon valley to Builth Wells. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.0005, -3.7931), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-3.7931 52.0005, -3.7746 52.0112, -3.7588 52.0233, -3.7456 52.0364, -3.7345 52.0489, -3.7157 52.0592, -3.7039 52.0712, -3.6878 52.0812, -3.6658 52.0911, -3.6457 52.1015, -3.631 52.114, -3.6154 52.1271, -3.6005 52.1395, -3.582 52.1491, -3.5634 52.1393, -3.5433 52.134, -3.5199 52.1391, -3.4952 52.1428, -3.4705 52.1472, -3.4482 52.1513, -3.4225 52.1495, -3.404 52.1495)'), 23.5, null, 'Mid Wales', array['Camera vans reported on Builth Wells bike-show weekends (BestBikingRoads); timber lorries; farm traffic; 30 mph through the towns.']::text[]),
  ('mw-a498-nant-gwynant', 'drive', 'A498 Nant Gwynant (Pen-y-Gwryd to Beddgelert)', 'From the Pen-y-Gwryd hotel down past Llyn Gwynant and Llyn Dinas through the Nant Gwynant valley to Beddgelert. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(53.0807, -4.0026), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-4.0026 53.0807, -4.0022 53.0653, -4.0089 53.0514, -4.0289 53.0431, -4.0489 53.0345, -4.0693 53.0245, -4.0925 53.0181, -4.1027 53.0117)'), 7.4, null, 'Eryri (Snowdonia)', array['Narrow with tight bends and stone walls; tourist traffic and coaches; walkers and campers around the lakes; Beddgelert is very busy in summer.']::text[]),
  ('mw-a5-ogwen', 'drive', 'A5 Nant Ffrancon (Capel Curig to Bethesda)', 'West from Capel Curig along Llyn Ogwen between the Carneddau and the Glyderau, then down the Nant Ffrancon pass to Bethesda. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(53.1046, -3.9139), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-3.9139 53.1046, -3.9254 53.1155, -3.9558 53.1227, -3.9818 53.1253, -4.0069 53.122, -4.0261 53.131, -4.0343 53.1458, -4.0441 53.1605, -4.0561 53.1731, -4.0575 53.1821)'), 9.9, null, 'Eryri (Snowdonia)', array['Mobile safety cameras, especially where 60 limits drop to 30 (BestBikingRoads); police bikes; walkers parked along Llyn Ogwen; sheep at the road edge; heavy summer traffic.']::text[]),
  ('mw-b4391-milltir-gerrig', 'drive', 'B4391 Bala to Llangynog (Milltir Gerrig)', 'South-east from Bala over the Berwyn moors and the Milltir Gerrig pass (486 m), then the steep drop into the Tanat valley at Llangynog. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.9084, -3.5927), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-3.5927 52.9084, -3.5774 52.9042, -3.5531 52.9077, -3.5303 52.9055, -3.5153 52.9041, -3.4943 52.8971, -3.4814 52.8841, -3.4706 52.872, -3.4569 52.8587, -3.4345 52.8509, -3.4202 52.838, -3.4059 52.8258, -3.4024 52.8265)'), 12.4, null, 'North Wales', array['Blind crests with sheep beyond them; fog and frost on the top; gravel after rain; the Llangynog side is steep with tight bends.']::text[]),
  ('mw-a4212', 'drive', 'A4212 Bala to Trawsfynydd', 'West from Bala past Frongoch and along Llyn Celyn, then over the moors to Trawsfynydd. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.9147, -3.6006), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-3.6006 52.9147, -3.6137 52.9281, -3.6313 52.9399, -3.6533 52.9477, -3.6825 52.9512, -3.7084 52.9548, -3.7212 52.9571, -3.7293 52.9448, -3.7552 52.9422, -3.7755 52.9322, -3.8002 52.9301, -3.8216 52.9259, -3.8424 52.9155, -3.8647 52.9086, -3.8906 52.9064, -3.9159 52.9021, -3.923 52.902)'), 17.6, null, 'Eryri (Snowdonia)', array['Police at weekends (BestBikingRoads); some unforgiving bends with drops beside them; summer holiday traffic; sheep on the open sections.']::text[]),
  ('mw-a487-cross-foxes', 'drive', 'A487 Dolgellau to Machynlleth', 'Out of Dolgellau on the A470 to Cross Foxes, then the A487 over the pass below Cadair Idris, past Tal-y-llyn and down through Corris to Machynlleth. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.7398, -3.8778), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-3.8778 52.7398, -3.8616 52.7458, -3.8402 52.7456, -3.8287 52.7331, -3.8348 52.7178, -3.8498 52.7035, -3.8665 52.691, -3.879 52.6784, -3.8659 52.665, -3.8497 52.6547, -3.8448 52.641, -3.8432 52.6313, -3.8495 52.6185, -3.8457 52.604, -3.853 52.5899)'), 16, null, 'Eryri (Snowdonia)', array['Tight bends near Machynlleth; caravans and holiday traffic; Corris village.']::text[]),
  ('mw-dylife', 'drive', 'Machynlleth to Llanidloes via Dylife', 'The mountain road from Machynlleth past the Wynford Vaughan-Thomas memorial and the old Dylife mines, then the B4518 past Llyn Clywedog to Llanidloes. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.5917, -3.8465), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-3.8465 52.5917, -3.8262 52.584, -3.8058 52.5756, -3.7806 52.5713, -3.7636 52.5632, -3.7399 52.5562, -3.7181 52.5489, -3.7052 52.5378, -3.6834 52.5324, -3.6573 52.5319, -3.6468 52.5207, -3.6304 52.5094, -3.6264 52.4944, -3.6027 52.4873, -3.5897 52.476, -3.5689 52.4676, -3.5491 52.4579, -3.5411 52.4489)'), 19, null, 'Mid Wales', array['Narrow mountain road, often closed or slippery in winter; sheep and cattle grids; farm traffic on the B4518; no fuel between the towns.']::text[]),
  ('mw-gower', 'drive', 'Gower: A4118 and B4247 to Rhossili', 'West across Fairwood Common on the A4118 South Gower Road through Parkmill and Penmaen to Scurlage, then the B4247 to Rhossili. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.6152, -4.0454), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-4.0454 51.6152, -4.0608 51.6043, -4.0708 51.5895, -4.0908 51.5823, -4.1157 51.5796, -4.1331 51.5755, -4.1586 51.5751, -4.181 51.5798, -4.2062 51.5794, -4.2205 51.5711, -4.2324 51.5623, -4.2539 51.565, -4.2774 51.567, -4.2858 51.5691)'), 13.9, null, 'Gower', array['Ponies, sheep and cattle graze the open commons; narrow lanes and summer beach traffic; Rhossili car park fills early in summer. Swansea council orders were not checked (see Avoid).', 'Medium confidence: the line or the source is partial (see the research notes). Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('mw-a487-pembrokeshire', 'drive', 'A487 St Davids to Fishguard', 'North-east from St Davids through Croes-goch and Mathry to Fishguard, inland of the coast path. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(51.8814, -5.2676), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-5.2676 51.8814, -5.2457 51.8884, -5.2223 51.8974, -5.2 51.9054, -5.1805 51.9146, -5.163 51.9274, -5.1393 51.9347, -5.1143 51.9397, -5.088 51.9429, -5.0649 51.9506, -5.0456 51.9605, -5.0245 51.9714, -5.0089 51.9821, -4.9871 51.9885, -4.976 51.994)'), 15.6, null, 'Pembrokeshire', array['Villages and 30 mph limits; tractors and caravans; narrow in places; St Davids is busy in summer.', 'Medium confidence: the line or the source is partial (see the research notes). Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('mw-a4117-clee-hill', 'drive', 'A4117 Ludlow to Cleobury Mortimer (Clee Hill)', 'East from Ludlow up Angel Bank to Cleehill village on the slopes of Titterstone Clee, across the common and down Hopton Bank to Cleobury Mortimer. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.3738, -2.6933), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-2.6933 52.3738, -2.6816 52.3825, -2.6584 52.3805, -2.6332 52.3806, -2.6078 52.3768, -2.5858 52.3794, -2.563 52.3848, -2.5393 52.3839, -2.5144 52.3771, -2.4888 52.3783, -2.4819 52.3792)'), 10.5, null, 'Shropshire Hills', array['Open common with cattle grids and grazing sheep; often affected by snow; steep Angel Bank and Hopton Bank; 30 mph through Cleehill.']::text[]),
  ('mw-b4363', 'drive', 'B4363 Cleobury Mortimer to Bridgnorth', 'North through forest and farmland from Cleobury Mortimer to Bridgnorth. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.3792, -2.4819), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-2.4819 52.3792, -2.4703 52.3898, -2.4539 52.4016, -2.4336 52.4115, -2.4137 52.4209, -2.412 52.4373, -2.4244 52.4494, -2.4296 52.4631, -2.4435 52.4753, -2.4424 52.4902, -2.4319 52.5041, -2.4335 52.5185, -2.4188 52.5305, -2.4198 52.533)'), 13.8, null, 'Shropshire', array['Leaves and mud in the forest sections in autumn; blind dips; farm traffic.']::text[]),
  ('mw-b4204', 'drive', 'B4204 Worcester to Tenbury Wells', 'West from the edge of Worcester through Martley and Clifton upon Teme, past the Shelsley Walsh hill climb turn, to Tenbury Wells. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.2031, -2.2449), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-2.2449 52.2031, -2.2692 52.2076, -2.2901 52.218, -2.3134 52.224, -2.3355 52.2299, -2.3547 52.2376, -2.3759 52.2437, -2.397 52.2444, -2.4144 52.2502, -2.4287 52.2621, -2.4442 52.2717, -2.4636 52.2812, -2.4867 52.2849, -2.5068 52.2936, -2.53 52.298, -2.5488 52.3036, -2.5743 52.3079, -2.5947 52.3101)'), 19.1, null, 'Worcestershire', array['Narrow village sections; farm traffic; mud on the road; no fast stretches.']::text[]),
  ('mw-a488', 'drive', 'A488 Bishop''s Castle to Knighton', 'South from Bishop''s Castle through Clun and over the hills to Knighton on the Welsh border. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.4929, -2.9991), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-2.9991 52.4929, -3.0023 52.4802, -3.0116 52.4651, -3.0237 52.4519, -3.0359 52.4383, -3.0314 52.4231, -3.0425 52.4108, -3.0442 52.3951, -3.0414 52.3805, -3.0461 52.3668, -3.0361 52.3541, -3.0377 52.3452, -3.048 52.344)'), 12.9, null, 'Shropshire Hills', array['Blind bends and crests; farm traffic and mud; Clun village is narrow.']::text[]),
  ('mw-a53-leek-buxton', 'drive', 'A53 Leek to Buxton (Ramshaw Rocks)', 'North from Leek past the Roaches and Ramshaw Rocks, over the moors past Flash to the edge of Buxton. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(53.1078, -2.0239), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-2.0239 53.1078, -2.004 53.1129, -1.9936 53.128, -1.9826 53.1428, -1.9708 53.1572, -1.9614 53.1734, -1.9553 53.1888, -1.9563 53.2046, -1.9508 53.2202, -1.9443 53.2354, -1.9383 53.2503, -1.9355 53.2526)'), 11.5, null, 'Peak District', array['Rated a high-risk road for serious collisions in a EuroRAP report (Wikipedia, A53); bends and crests over open moor; police enforcement; snow and fog.', 'Medium confidence: the line or the source is partial (see the research notes). Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('mw-b6047', 'drive', 'B6047 Market Harborough to Melton Mowbray', 'North through the High Leicestershire hills via the Langtons, Tilton on the Hill, Twyford and Great Dalby to Melton Mowbray. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.4806, -0.9238), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-0.9238 52.4806, -0.937 52.4943, -0.9419 52.5097, -0.938 52.5264, -0.9444 52.5409, -0.9416 52.5558, -0.942 52.5727, -0.9346 52.5892, -0.9338 52.6047, -0.9228 52.6192, -0.9161 52.6343, -0.9036 52.6464, -0.9178 52.6573, -0.9329 52.67, -0.9255 52.6822, -0.918 52.6943, -0.9108 52.7094, -0.8961 52.7205, -0.8867 52.7354, -0.8898 52.7505, -0.8874 52.7596)'), 22.3, null, 'Leicestershire', array['50 mph limit south of the A47 (BestBikingRoads); blind corners and crests; village 30s.']::text[]),
  ('mw-a6003', 'drive', 'A6003 Corby to Oakham (Rutland)', 'North from Rockingham Hill past Caldecott to Uppingham, then on to Oakham near Rutland Water. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(52.51, -0.7174), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-0.7174 52.51, -0.7249 52.5247, -0.7213 52.5393, -0.7278 52.554, -0.7288 52.5698, -0.7227 52.5859, -0.723 52.5986, -0.7128 52.6129, -0.7087 52.6287, -0.709 52.6438, -0.7195 52.6591)'), 11.4, null, 'Rutland', array['Speed camera where the road leaves Corby (BestBikingRoads); hidden T-junctions; police interest reported.']::text[]),
  ('mw-p-bwlch-y-groes', 'photo', 'Bwlch y Groes summit', 'Parking area at the top of the pass by the cross, with views to Aran Fawddwy and the Dyfi valley. The car makers'' old test hill ("Hellfire Pass", Wikipedia); BestBikingRoads riders stop at the top for the view.', private.pt(52.796, -3.6131), null, null, null, 'Eryri (Snowdonia)', array['Small parking area; single-track road – don''t block passing places; exposed in bad weather.', 'Medium confidence: the position is approximate or the details are not confirmed for 2026. Check before you go.']::text[]),
  ('mw-p-black-mountain', 'photo', 'Black Mountain Pass summit viewpoint (A4069)', 'The viewing point and parking at the top of the A4069 over the Black Mountain. BestBikingRoads: riders pause at the summit viewing point to chat and let brakes cool. The road itself is already a Drive.', private.pt(51.8576, -3.8492), null, null, null, 'Bannau Brycheiniog (Brecon Beacons)', array['40 mph average-speed cameras along the whole road since about 2023 (BestBikingRoads review, 2024); position is approximate; sheep.', 'Medium confidence: the position is approximate or the details are not confirmed for 2026. Check before you go.']::text[]),
  ('mw-p-llyn-gwynant', 'photo', 'Llyn Gwynant (A498)', 'Parking on the A498 beside Llyn Gwynant, below Snowdon. BestBikingRoads: a pull-in by the lake with terrific views of Snowdon; one of the most photographed views in Snowdonia (Wikipedia).', private.pt(53.0457, -4.0212), null, null, null, 'Eryri (Snowdonia)', array['Busy with campers and paddlers in summer; position is the lakeside car park, not a set viewpoint; don''t stop on the road.', 'Medium confidence: the position is approximate or the details are not confirmed for 2026. Check before you go.']::text[]),
  ('mw-p-wvt-memorial', 'photo', 'Wynford Vaughan-Thomas memorial', 'Viewpoint with a memorial on the Machynlleth–Dylife mountain road. BestBikingRoads: the stop on the Machynlleth–Dylife ride, with excellent views.', private.pt(52.5489, -3.7183), null, null, null, 'Mid Wales', array['Small pull-off on a narrow mountain road; road can be closed or icy in winter.', 'Medium confidence: the position is approximate or the details are not confirmed for 2026. Check before you go.']::text[]),
  ('mw-p-devils-bridge', 'photo', 'Devil''s Bridge (Pontarfynach)', 'Car park by the three stacked bridges and the falls at Devil''s Bridge, at the end of the Elan Valley mountain road. BestBikingRoads: "a popular haunt with bikers"; the falls and the Punchbowl are a coin-operated visit.', private.pt(52.3773, -3.849), null, null, null, 'Mid Wales', array['Pay parking; busy with coaches and visitors in summer; narrow bridge on the A4120.']::text[]),
  ('sni-applecross-coast', 'drive', 'Applecross coast road (Applecross to Shieldaig)', 'The long way round the Applecross peninsula: north along the Inner Sound past Fearnmore, then east along Loch Torridon via Kenmore and Ardheslaig to the A896 by Shieldaig. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(57.4328, -5.8094), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-5.8094 57.4328, -5.8096 57.443, -5.8378 57.4415, -5.8594 57.4493, -5.8621 57.4653, -5.8632 57.4806, -5.8605 57.4965, -5.8582 57.5138, -5.8518 57.5287, -5.8437 57.5433, -5.832 57.5553, -5.8206 57.5693, -5.8018 57.5747, -5.7861 57.5655, -5.7691 57.5568, -5.7553 57.5498, -5.7413 57.537, -5.7253 57.5409, -5.7079 57.5395, -5.6915 57.529, -5.6714 57.5202, -5.6526 57.5103, -5.6474 57.5162, -5.6504 57.5236)'), 25.2, null, 'Wester Ross', array['Single-track with passing places: pull into a passing place on your left (or wait opposite one on your right) for oncoming traffic and to let faster vehicles past, and never park in one (Police Scotland/NC500 advice). Blind crests and tight bends; sheep and deer on the road; very remote with no phone signal in places (BestBikingRoads); slow camper traffic in summer.', 'Medium confidence: the line or the source is partial (see the research notes). Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sni-a896-torridon', 'drive', 'A896 Lochcarron to Kinlochewe via Torridon', 'Round Loch Kishorn past the Bealach na Bà turn at Tornapress, over to Shieldaig, along Upper Loch Torridon and up Glen Torridon under Liathach and Beinn Eighe to Kinlochewe. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(57.4005, -5.4906), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-5.4906 57.4005, -5.5089 57.4025, -5.5369 57.4059, -5.5661 57.4047, -5.5932 57.3994, -5.6092 57.4081, -5.5993 57.4259, -5.5856 57.4398, -5.5847 57.4541, -5.5858 57.4689, -5.6007 57.4824, -5.6195 57.4946, -5.6365 57.5065, -5.6472 57.5202, -5.6298 57.5218, -5.6104 57.5296, -5.5866 57.5264, -5.5575 57.5278, -5.5291 57.5271, -5.5065 57.5354, -5.4877 57.5404, -5.4627 57.5491, -5.4359 57.5533, -5.4083 57.5565, -5.3845 57.5647, -5.3577 57.5664, -5.3317 57.5725, -5.3109 57.586, -5.3055 57.6017, -5.3051 57.604)'), 32, null, 'Wester Ross', array['Single-track with passing places: pull into a passing place on your left (or wait opposite one on your right) for oncoming traffic and to let faster vehicles past, and never park in one (Police Scotland/NC500 advice). Long single-track sections between Shieldaig and Kinlochewe; walkers'' cars parked at Glen Torridon trailheads; deer, especially at dusk.', 'Medium confidence: the line or the source is partial (see the research notes). Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sni-a832-loch-maree', 'drive', 'A832 Loch Maree (Kinlochewe to Gairloch)', 'Along the south shore of Loch Maree under Slioch, through the Slattadale forest and down to Gairloch. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(57.604, -5.3), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-5.3 57.604, -5.3206 57.616, -5.342 57.627, -5.3649 57.6364, -5.3849 57.6487, -5.4095 57.6538, -5.4325 57.6628, -5.4584 57.6717, -5.4855 57.6752, -5.5097 57.6804, -5.5393 57.6828, -5.5607 57.6925, -5.5894 57.6888, -5.6173 57.6869, -5.6438 57.6855, -5.6569 57.6948, -5.6735 57.7068, -5.6863 57.7203, -5.6941 57.7282)'), 20, null, 'Wester Ross', array['Mostly two-way but with a single-track section near Gairloch – use passing places properly; deer; NC500 campervans; police and marked motorcycle patrols run enforcement weekends on the NC500 (Operation Cedar).']::text[]),
  ('sni-a832-gruinard', 'drive', 'A832 Gruinard Bay (Poolewe to Corrie Hallie)', 'From Poolewe past Aultbea and Laide, round Gruinard Bay with its beaches, then along Little Loch Broom to Dundonnell and Corrie Hallie. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(57.765, -5.5989), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-5.5989 57.765, -5.5925 57.7774, -5.5745 57.7892, -5.5788 57.802, -5.5779 57.8134, -5.5777 57.8274, -5.575 57.8388, -5.5577 57.8505, -5.5425 57.8644, -5.514 57.8631, -5.49 57.8548, -5.4686 57.85, -5.4481 57.8574, -5.4397 57.8705, -5.4274 57.8809, -5.399 57.8846, -5.3714 57.8795, -5.3419 57.8703, -5.3167 57.8615, -5.2893 57.8548, -5.2617 57.85, -5.2326 57.844, -5.2045 57.8377, -5.1854 57.8268, -5.1782 57.82)'), 26.6, null, 'Wester Ross', array['Single-track in places with passing places; blind crests round Gruinard; sheep and deer; summer NC500 traffic and campervans stopping at the viewpoints.']::text[]),
  ('sni-a890-stromeferry', 'drive', 'A890 Strathcarron to Auchtertyre (Stromeferry)', 'Along the south shore of Loch Carron under rock cuttings at Stromeferry, then over the hill to Auchtertyre on the A87 near Eilean Donan. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(57.4315, -5.4468), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-5.4468 57.4315, -5.4302 57.4202, -5.4471 57.4074, -5.4552 57.3931, -5.4745 57.3817, -5.4978 57.3722, -5.5158 57.3593, -5.537 57.3486, -5.5612 57.3446, -5.5397 57.3367, -5.5456 57.3216, -5.5572 57.3079, -5.5658 57.2944, -5.5813 57.2858)'), 14.6, null, 'Wester Ross', array['Steep rock cuttings above the loch – check Highland Council for closures; steep climbs and descents over the hill; deer; little traffic so animals linger on the road.']::text[]),
  ('sni-a894-kylesku', 'drive', 'A894 Assynt: Skiag Bridge to Scourie (Kylesku Bridge)', 'North from Loch Assynt over the moor, down to the curved Kylesku Bridge across Loch a'' Chàirn Bhàin, then across the lochan-studded country to Scourie. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(58.1773, -5.0282), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-5.0282 58.1773, -5.0023 58.1743, -5.0126 58.188, -5.0069 58.2028, -5 58.2161, -5.0082 58.2289, -5.0072 58.2423, -5.0211 58.2524, -5.039 58.2612, -5.0579 58.2721, -5.0749 58.2853, -5.1023 58.2966, -5.1214 58.3067, -5.1262 58.3217, -5.1352 58.336, -5.1585 58.3428, -5.1529 58.3518)'), 17.8, null, 'Sutherland', array['Blind crests and narrow sections; sheep and deer on unfenced road; NC500 traffic in summer; exposed bridge in high winds.']::text[]),
  ('sni-a838-eriboll', 'drive', 'A838 Durness to Tongue (Loch Eriboll)', 'East from Durness, right round Loch Eriboll, over the Moine and across the Kyle of Tongue causeway to Tongue. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(58.566, -4.7462), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-4.7462 58.566, -4.7268 58.5642, -4.7063 58.5553, -4.6813 58.549, -4.6762 58.5364, -4.6851 58.5217, -4.7013 58.5093, -4.7186 58.4966, -4.7304 58.4819, -4.745 58.4679, -4.7593 58.4546, -4.7454 58.4448, -4.7268 58.4557, -4.7036 58.4611, -4.6827 58.4704, -4.6696 58.482, -4.6608 58.4938, -4.6461 58.5023, -4.6241 58.5042, -4.6025 58.5062, -4.5757 58.502, -4.5469 58.5048, -4.5173 58.5035, -4.4881 58.5017, -4.4619 58.4976, -4.4341 58.4923, -4.4183 58.4818, -4.4188 58.4779)'), 29.5, null, 'Sutherland', array['Single-track with passing places: pull into a passing place on your left (or wait opposite one on your right) for oncoming traffic and to let faster vehicles past, and never park in one (Police Scotland/NC500 advice). Long single-track stretches; very remote (few services between Durness and Tongue); sheep and deer; exposed causeway in high winds.']::text[]),
  ('sni-a836-caithness', 'drive', 'A836 Caithness coast (Thurso to John o'' Groats)', 'East from Thurso past Castletown and Dunnet Bay (turn for Dunnet Head, the mainland''s most northerly point), then Mey and the Castle of Mey to John o'' Groats. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(58.5951, -3.5204), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-3.5204 58.5951, -3.5024 58.5942, -3.4708 58.5931, -3.4393 58.5943, -3.4086 58.5954, -3.3817 58.5922, -3.3541 58.5978, -3.3435 58.6133, -3.3277 58.627, -3.2982 58.631, -3.2675 58.6335, -3.2366 58.6357, -3.2089 58.6451, -3.1782 58.6418, -3.151 58.6368, -3.1187 58.6385, -3.0892 58.6423, -3.0688 58.64)'), 19.8, null, 'Caithness', array['Mostly two-lane here (other parts of the A836 are single-track); exposed to strong crosswinds off the Pentland Firth; slow tourist traffic near Dunnet Head and John o'' Groats; 30 mph villages.', 'Medium confidence: the line or the source is partial (see the research notes). Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sni-a9-berriedale', 'drive', 'A9 Helmsdale to Dunbeath (Berriedale Braes)', 'North from Helmsdale over the Ord of Caithness, down and up the Berriedale Braes and along the clifftops to Dunbeath. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(58.1179, -3.6485), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-3.6485 58.1179, -3.633 58.1281, -3.6095 58.1373, -3.5989 58.1462, -3.5888 58.1598, -3.5624 58.1632, -3.5336 58.1699, -3.5099 58.179, -3.4978 58.1877, -3.48 58.1997, -3.4785 58.2151, -3.4539 58.2251, -3.445 58.2394, -3.4259 58.2495)'), 15, 60, 'Caithness', array['Steep gradients and tight bends at the Ord and Berriedale – HGVs crawl on the climbs; the main road north, so expect lorries and campervans; crosswinds on the clifftops; deer.']::text[]),
  ('sni-a855-trotternish', 'drive', 'A855 Trotternish (Portree to Staffin)', 'North from Portree under the Storr and the Old Man of Storr, past the lochs and the Kilt Rock coast to Staffin. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(57.413, -6.195), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-6.195 57.413, -6.1883 57.4238, -6.1822 57.4383, -6.1818 57.4543, -6.1834 57.47, -6.175 57.4851, -6.1592 57.4974, -6.1514 57.5126, -6.1566 57.528, -6.1457 57.542, -6.1539 57.5572, -6.1533 57.572, -6.1573 57.588, -6.1678 57.6028, -6.1854 57.6151, -6.2052 57.6228)'), 16.7, null, 'Isle of Skye', array['Narrow with blind bends and single-track sections; very busy with coaches and cars at the Storr and Kilt Rock in summer – never stop on the verge; sheep; Portree is congested.', 'Medium confidence: the line or the source is partial (see the research notes). Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sni-a830-road-to-the-isles', 'drive', 'A830 Road to the Isles (Fort William to Mallaig)', 'West from Banavie past Corpach and along Loch Eil to Glenfinnan, then Loch Eilt, Lochailort, Arisaig and the Morar sands to the ferry port at Mallaig. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(56.8459, -5.0948), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-5.0948 56.8459, -5.1225 56.8439, -5.1513 56.8448, -5.176 56.8531, -5.2049 56.8557, -5.2346 56.8552, -5.2642 56.8546, -5.2931 56.8564, -5.3215 56.8597, -5.351 56.86, -5.3793 56.8622, -5.404 56.8599, -5.4271 56.8677, -5.4525 56.8728, -5.478 56.8786, -5.5061 56.8758, -5.5294 56.8772, -5.5548 56.8783, -5.5801 56.8811, -5.6074 56.8832, -5.6318 56.8853, -5.6585 56.8828, -5.6822 56.8804, -5.7076 56.8872, -5.7312 56.8927, -5.7561 56.8936, -5.765 56.9002, -5.7932 56.8989, -5.82 56.9064, -5.8386 56.9113, -5.85 56.9246, -5.8413 56.9405, -5.8291 56.9544, -5.8237 56.9673, -5.8273 56.983, -5.8331 56.9979, -5.8292 57.0051)'), 39.9, null, 'Lochaber', array['Glenfinnan is gridlocked in summer by viaduct and Jacobite steam-train visitors – use the paid car park only; a stretch of poorer surface (BestBikingRoads); deer; ferry traffic towards Mallaig. Skye ferry from Mallaig must be booked.']::text[]),
  ('sni-a87-glengarry', 'drive', 'A87 Invergarry to Cluanie (Glen Garry)', 'West from the A82 at Invergarry along Loch Garry, over the high ground by Loch Loyne and down to Loch Cluanie – it joins the existing Glen Shiel drive at Cluanie. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(57.0698, -4.7925), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-4.7925 57.0698, -4.8209 57.0675, -4.8353 57.0747, -4.859 57.0814, -4.8869 57.0818, -4.9149 57.0831, -4.9439 57.0819, -4.9699 57.0874, -4.9934 57.0943, -4.9848 57.1085, -4.9725 57.1221, -4.9556 57.1345, -4.9635 57.1454, -4.9919 57.1456, -5.0207 57.1485, -5.0493 57.1482, -5.0731 57.1426, -5.1002 57.1473, -5.1057 57.1467)'), 19.3, 60, 'Lochaber', array['Main route to Skye – heavy summer traffic and coaches; deer; snow and ice on the high section by Loch Loyne in winter; long gaps between fuel.']::text[]),
  ('sni-b862-south-loch-ness', 'drive', 'South Loch Ness: B862/B852 Fort Augustus to Dores', 'General Wade''s Military Road out of Fort Augustus over the hills past Loch Tarff to Whitebridge, then down to Foyers and along the quiet south shore of Loch Ness to Dores. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(57.1447, -4.6799), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-4.6799 57.1447, -4.661 57.1385, -4.6378 57.1438, -4.6138 57.1474, -4.5882 57.1536, -4.5622 57.1608, -4.5456 57.1756, -4.5278 57.1885, -4.5098 57.2011, -4.4966 57.2128, -4.4817 57.2248, -4.4736 57.2372, -4.4839 57.246, -4.4665 57.2586, -4.4494 57.2717, -4.4536 57.2845, -4.4385 57.298, -4.4225 57.3112, -4.4065 57.3254, -4.3842 57.3384, -4.3639 57.3541, -4.3478 57.3688, -4.3325 57.3804)'), 25.1, null, 'Great Glen', array['Single-track sections with blind corners, especially from Fort Augustus to Foyers and near Dores – extra care on corners; deer; walkers and cyclists on the South Loch Ness Trail.', 'Medium confidence: the line or the source is partial (see the research notes). Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sni-a86-laggan', 'drive', 'A86 Spean Bridge to Newtonmore (Loch Laggan)', 'East from Spean Bridge through Roybridge and Glen Spean, along Loch Laggan past the Laggan Dam, then Laggan and down the Spey to Newtonmore. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(56.8904, -4.9199), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-4.9199 56.8904, -4.8976 56.8948, -4.8701 56.8908, -4.8416 56.8909, -4.8137 56.8858, -4.7886 56.889, -4.7613 56.8892, -4.7331 56.8901, -4.7064 56.888, -4.6781 56.8903, -4.6537 56.8977, -4.6251 56.9005, -4.5989 56.9073, -4.571 56.9134, -4.5456 56.9266, -4.5208 56.9343, -4.5012 56.9458, -4.4801 56.9556, -4.4534 56.9635, -4.4283 56.9718, -4.4023 56.9758, -4.3767 56.9783, -4.3517 56.9842, -4.3268 56.9911, -4.3135 57.0058, -4.2895 57.0122, -4.266 57.0194, -4.2373 57.0176, -4.2117 57.0238, -4.1903 57.0307, -4.167 57.0397, -4.1487 57.0527, -4.1275 57.0628, -4.1197 57.0635)'), 36.8, null, 'Highlands', array['Visitors stopping suddenly for views (BestBikingRoads); deer; some narrow sections between Laggan and Newtonmore; snow on the high ground in winter.']::text[]),
  ('sni-sma-glen', 'drive', 'Sma'' Glen: A822/A826 Gilmerton to Aberfeldy', 'North from Gilmerton through the Sma'' Glen (Glen Almond), over to Amulree, then the A826 down Glen Cochill to Aberfeldy. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(56.3919, -3.8069), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-3.8069 56.3919, -3.8077 56.4075, -3.7875 56.4201, -3.7641 56.431, -3.7773 56.4443, -3.7958 56.4558, -3.8007 56.4672, -3.8006 56.4822, -3.7872 56.4963, -3.7876 56.51, -3.7641 56.5168, -3.763 56.528, -3.7775 56.5407, -3.778 56.5566, -3.7935 56.5701, -3.8131 56.5818, -3.825 56.596, -3.8329 56.6057, -3.8492 56.615, -3.8651 56.62)'), 21.6, null, 'Perthshire', array['Popular with bikers, so expect police attention at weekends; sheep on the unfenced moor; cyclists; snow on the high ground by Amulree.']::text[]),
  ('sni-a821-dukes-pass', 'drive', 'Duke''s Pass (A821), Aberfoyle to Callander', 'Up the hairpins out of Aberfoyle over the Duke''s Pass (240 m), down past Loch Achray and Brig o'' Turk, then along Loch Venachar to Callander. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(56.1792, -4.383), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-4.383 56.1792, -4.3845 56.1885, -4.3925 56.2015, -4.385 56.2121, -4.4013 56.2216, -4.4105 56.2314, -4.3874 56.2276, -4.3613 56.2297, -4.3344 56.2269, -4.3059 56.2254, -4.278 56.2295, -4.2556 56.2385, -4.2407 56.2463, -4.2148 56.244)'), 14.5, null, 'Trossachs', array['Big coaches and slow tourist traffic – quieter in the early evening (BestBikingRoads); gravel from patching; Three Lochs Forest Drive and car-park traffic; Loch Lomond & The Trossachs National Park byelaws in summer.']::text[]),
  ('sni-a917-east-neuk', 'drive', 'A917 East Neuk of Fife (Elie to St Andrews)', 'Along the East Neuk fishing villages – Elie, St Monans, Pittenweem, Anstruther, Crail – then round Fife Ness and up the coast to St Andrews. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(56.1903, -2.8199), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-2.8199 56.1903, -2.7948 56.1972, -2.7731 56.2073, -2.7469 56.2127, -2.72 56.2165, -2.7012 56.2236, -2.6838 56.2351, -2.6594 56.2439, -2.6359 56.2548, -2.6362 56.2668, -2.6449 56.2818, -2.6586 56.2974, -2.6724 56.3105, -2.6987 56.3123, -2.7237 56.3137, -2.7504 56.3217, -2.776 56.3293, -2.7955 56.338)'), 19.4, null, 'Fife', array['Many 20/30 mph village limits and narrow main streets; tourist and golf traffic around St Andrews; farm traffic; cyclists on the coastal route.', 'Medium confidence: the line or the source is partial (see the research notes). Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sni-a712-queens-way', 'drive', 'Queen''s Way (A712) New Galloway to Newton Stewart', 'The Queen''s Way through the Galloway Forest Park, past Clatteringshaws Loch and Murray''s Monument, down to Newton Stewart. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(55.0758, -4.1441), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-4.1441 55.0758, -4.1647 55.0716, -4.1908 55.0734, -4.2167 55.0696, -4.2437 55.0676, -4.2681 55.061, -4.2792 55.0467, -4.2992 55.0369, -4.3221 55.0284, -4.3453 55.0209, -4.3669 55.016, -4.3852 55.0048, -4.4035 54.9927, -4.4237 54.9844, -4.4393 54.9731, -4.4539 54.9608, -4.457 54.9578)'), 17, null, 'Galloway', array['Timber lorries in the forest; deer and wild goats; red squirrels; sheep; Dark Sky Park – very dark at night; check surface after forestry works.']::text[]),
  ('sni-a708-moffat-selkirk', 'drive', 'A708 Moffat to Selkirk (St Mary''s Loch)', 'North-east out of Moffat up the Moffat Water past the Grey Mare''s Tail, over to St Mary''s Loch and down the Yarrow valley to Selkirk. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(55.3329, -3.4406), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-3.4406 55.3329, -3.4155 55.3283, -3.3943 55.3327, -3.3788 55.3451, -3.3626 55.3582, -3.3528 55.3729, -3.3333 55.3835, -3.3185 55.3967, -3.3002 55.4086, -3.2813 55.4202, -3.2621 55.4319, -3.2415 55.441, -3.2219 55.4499, -3.2109 55.4647, -3.2085 55.4799, -3.2039 55.4952, -3.1772 55.4999, -3.1526 55.5079, -3.1238 55.5093, -3.0956 55.5132, -3.0679 55.5182, -3.0426 55.5231, -3.0314 55.5369, -3.0066 55.5393, -2.9857 55.5492, -2.9631 55.5564, -2.9355 55.5596, -2.9115 55.5527, -2.8956 55.54, -2.8699 55.5429, -2.8479 55.5472, -2.8399 55.547)'), 34.3, null, 'Scottish Borders', array['Sharp crests and tight bends at the Moffat end; gravelly surfaces; sheep; walkers parking at the Grey Mare''s Tail (National Trust for Scotland car park).']::text[]),
  ('sni-a701-beef-tub', 'drive', 'A701 Moffat to Broughton (Devil''s Beef Tub)', 'North from Moffat up the edge of the Devil''s Beef Tub, over the watershed and down the upper Tweed past Tweedsmuir to Broughton. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(55.3329, -3.4406), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-3.4406 55.3329, -3.4578 55.3406, -3.4699 55.3551, -3.4752 55.3692, -3.4847 55.3841, -3.484 55.3978, -3.5078 55.404, -3.5013 55.4186, -3.506 55.4305, -3.4993 55.4452, -3.4977 55.4611, -3.4906 55.4764, -3.4689 55.487, -3.4455 55.4985, -3.4248 55.5096, -3.4097 55.5228, -3.4129 55.538, -3.4068 55.5525, -3.3942 55.5662, -3.3987 55.5818, -3.406 55.5968, -3.4119 55.6102)'), 23.6, null, 'Scottish Borders', array['A few tight bends catch people out (BestBikingRoads); sheep; exposed and snowy at the Beef Tub summit; lay-by at the Beef Tub viewpoint only – don''t stop on the road.']::text[]),
  ('sni-a2-antrim-coast', 'drive', 'Antrim Coast Road (A2) Larne to Cushendall', 'The Antrim Coast Road north from Larne past Ballygally Head, Glenarm and Carnlough, round Garron Point to Waterfoot (Glenariff) and Cushendall. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(54.8617, -5.8086), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-5.8086 54.8617, -5.8218 54.8752, -5.8401 54.8858, -5.845 54.9008, -5.8687 54.9034, -5.8831 54.9158, -5.8917 54.9308, -5.9038 54.9451, -5.9169 54.9591, -5.9368 54.9696, -5.959 54.9712, -5.9759 54.9798, -5.9929 54.9887, -5.9841 55.0032, -5.9763 55.0175, -5.9712 55.0331, -5.9634 55.0482, -5.9846 55.0579, -6.0113 55.0568, -6.0378 55.054, -6.0599 55.061, -6.055 55.0752, -6.0642 55.0801)'), 24, null, 'County Antrim', array['Lined with unforgiving stone walls (BestBikingRoads); coaches and slow tourist traffic; villages at 30 mph; sea spray and rockfalls under the cliffs; busy around North West 200 week.']::text[]),
  ('sni-causeway-coast', 'drive', 'Causeway Coast (B15/A2) Ballycastle to Portrush', 'West from Ballycastle on the coast road past Ballintoy and Whitepark Bay, then the A2 by the Giant''s Causeway, Bushmills and Dunluce Castle to Portrush. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(55.2039, -6.2429), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-6.2429 55.2039, -6.2605 55.2114, -6.283 55.2147, -6.3101 55.2197, -6.3277 55.2314, -6.3503 55.2357, -6.3741 55.2354, -6.3991 55.2284, -6.4248 55.2306, -6.4513 55.2261, -6.4777 55.2219, -6.5066 55.2211, -6.5228 55.2088, -6.5456 55.2088, -6.5707 55.2123, -6.5941 55.2072, -6.6177 55.1999, -6.6442 55.2008, -6.6499 55.2)'), 19.5, null, 'County Antrim', array['Coaches and car-park queues at the Giant''s Causeway and Carrick-a-Rede; Bushmills village; PSNI run operations against car cruising and "diffing" around Portrush and Portstewart – no meets here.', 'Medium confidence: the line or the source is partial (see the research notes). Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sni-b27-spelga', 'drive', 'B27 Hilltown to Kilkeel past Spelga Dam', 'South-east from Hilltown up into the Mournes past Spelga Dam (about 370 m), across the high moor and down to Kilkeel on the coast. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(54.1977, -6.143), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-6.143 54.1977, -6.1191 54.1985, -6.0946 54.1921, -6.0721 54.1868, -6.0592 54.1794, -6.0497 54.1689, -6.0564 54.1536, -6.0512 54.1385, -6.0361 54.1254, -6.0288 54.1085, -6.0242 54.0927, -6.0159 54.0784, -5.9997 54.0658, -5.9966 54.0602)'), 14, null, 'Mourne Mountains', array['Mountain fog and snow; sheep on the open moor; cyclists; narrow single-lane approach roads from Bryansford (BestBikingRoads); Spelga car park busy on sunny weekends.', 'Medium confidence: the line or the source is partial (see the research notes). Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sni-a6-glenshane', 'drive', 'Glenshane Pass (A6)', 'The main Belfast–Derry road over the Sperrins: east from Dungiven up to the Glenshane Pass past the Ponderosa bar, then down to Maghera. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(54.9176, -6.9131), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-6.9131 54.9176, -6.8883 54.9106, -6.8614 54.9071, -6.835 54.9029, -6.8091 54.8982, -6.7906 54.8863, -6.7845 54.871, -6.7686 54.8582, -6.7429 54.8525, -6.716 54.8461, -6.7096 54.8447)'), 10.4, null, 'County Londonderry', array['Main trunk road with HGVs; exposed to snow and ice, often the first NI road affected in winter; speed limits enforced; fog on the summit.', 'Medium confidence: the line or the source is partial (see the research notes). Check it before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sni-b47-glenelly', 'drive', 'Glenelly Valley (B47), Sperrins', 'East up the Glenelly Valley, the longest in the Sperrins, past Cranagh and Goles under Sawel Mountain. Untimed: rep for finishing it within the limits.', private.pt(54.76, -7.2393), extensions.st_geogfromtext('SRID=4326;LINESTRING(-7.2393 54.76, -7.2442 54.769, -7.2174 54.7692, -7.1899 54.7677, -7.163 54.765, -7.136 54.767, -7.1098 54.7735, -7.0855 54.7809, -7.0834 54.7814, -7.0568 54.7857, -7.0297 54.7878, -7.0028 54.7936, -6.9755 54.7957, -6.9495 54.7932, -6.93 54.7896)'), 15.4, null, 'County Tyrone', array['Farm traffic and lots of driveways; bumpy surface and loose chippings in places; sheep; narrow in parts.']::text[]),
  ('sni-p-skyfall', 'photo', 'Glen Etive "Skyfall" lay-by', 'Lay-by about halfway down the single-track Glen Etive road where Bond''s Aston Martin DB5 stops in Skyfall; Glen Etive also starred in Volvo''s V90 advert. A popular stop for recreating the Skyfall car shot (Press and Journal).', private.pt(56.6195, -4.9307), null, null, null, 'Lochaber', array['Dead-end single-track road with passing places – never park in them; the National Trust for Scotland asks you to stop only in lay-bys and drive on if full (it plans to enlarge this one); deer; no phone signal.', 'Medium confidence: the position is approximate or the details are not confirmed for 2026. Check before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sni-p-storr', 'photo', 'Old Man of Storr car park', 'Car park beside the A855 below the Storr pinnacles, on the Trotternish drive. The Storr was one of the locations in Volvo''s V90 Cross Country advert (Press and Journal).', private.pt(57.4981, -6.1584), null, null, null, 'Isle of Skye', array['Pay car park that fills early in summer; do not park on the A855 verges; coach traffic.', 'Medium confidence: the position is approximate or the details are not confirmed for 2026. Check before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sni-p-kylesku', 'photo', 'Kylesku Bridge viewpoint', 'Pull-off with an information board by the north end of the curved Kylesku Bridge on the A894. Mazda shot its Highlands car campaign at sites around Kylesku and Gairloch (Little Black Book); the bridge is the A894 drive''s landmark.', private.pt(58.2567, -5.0212), null, null, null, 'Sutherland', array['Small parking area – pull fully off the A894; exposed to strong winds; NC500 campervans.', 'Medium confidence: the position is approximate or the details are not confirmed for 2026. Check before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sni-p-ballintoy', 'photo', 'Ballintoy Harbour', 'Small harbour car park at the bottom of the steep lane below Ballintoy village. Used for Mazda UK''s CX-3 press shoot on the Causeway Coast (photographer Tim Swart); also a Game of Thrones location.', private.pt(55.2439, -6.3695), null, null, null, 'County Antrim', array['Very steep, narrow lane with hairpins – not for large vehicles; small car park, busy with Game of Thrones tours; don''t drive onto the pier.', 'Medium confidence: the position is approximate or the details are not confirmed for 2026. Check before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sni-p-dunluce', 'photo', 'Dunluce Castle', 'Car park by the clifftop ruin of Dunluce Castle on the A2 between Bushmills and Portrush. The coast road seen from Dunluce Castle was one of the shots in Mazda UK''s CX-3 Causeway Coast shoot (photographer Tim Swart).', private.pt(55.2109, -6.576), null, null, null, 'County Antrim', array['Pull in and out of the A2 with care (fast road); castle visitor car park; close to the Portrush car-cruising hotspot – no meets.', 'Medium confidence: the position is approximate or the details are not confirmed for 2026. Check before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sni-p-torr-head', 'photo', 'Torr Head', 'Headland with a small parking area at the end of the Torr Head scenic road, looking across the North Channel to Kintyre. The road to Torr Head was photographed for Mazda UK''s CX-3 Causeway Coast shoot (photographer Tim Swart).', private.pt(55.196, -6.0632), null, null, null, 'County Antrim', array['The Torr Head road is very narrow, steep and twisty – not for caravans or large vehicles; tiny parking area; sheep.', 'Medium confidence: the position is approximate or the details are not confirmed for 2026. Check before you go.']::text[]),
  ('sni-p-spelga', 'photo', 'Spelga Dam car park', 'Car park and picnic area by Spelga Dam on the B27 high in the Mournes. A regular motorcycle stop – the Harley Owners Club NI branch used it as the first stop on its April 2026 Mournes run, and BestBikingRoads reviewers rate the road past the dam.', private.pt(54.1789, -6.058), null, null, null, 'Mourne Mountains', array['Exposed and often foggy; sheep; busy on sunny weekends.']::text[])
